{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce","id":1480216,"title":"Does anyone else dislike the Tzimisce?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-05T16:20:16-07:00","id":1480216,"title":"Does anyone else dislike the Tzimisce?","content":"Personally, I find the Tzimisce groaning. RAW basically turns what could have been a cool idea and infects them with CoolDisciplineitis and turns them into torturers and freak shows. <br /> <br /> Personally, I *like* the idea of the Old World monsters, adhering to ancient codes of conduct, who are gracious and painstakingly polite and are tied to the land and its inhabitants. Sadly, Vicissitude turns them into &quot;LOL now your bones are on the outside of your body for some reason and your flesh is globbed off because Dexterity + Body Crafts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I run them with Animalism, Auspex and Koldunic Sorcery as Clan Disciplines, because I enjoy the idea of the Magyar Sorcerers (Tzimisce) and the Hermetic Mages (Tremere) battling it out in some Shadow War to be far more appealing. I think it makes for a more compelling Clan and more compelling stories, where the Arcane realm is suddenly a battlefield, instead of just being the Tremere standing around earning favors by doing parlor tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T16:40:40-07:00","id":1480219,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this preface gets groan worthy... but my attachment to the Clans is heavily biased by my first experience with the game being Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Instead of the modern nights Tzimisce who combined Vicissitude and Sabbat membership into being splatterpunks with no real functional connection to the lords of the night they used to be, starting in the Dark Ages gave Vicissitude more of a sense of the Tzimisce being a contrast to the Venture and Lasombras as the being &quot;royal&quot; Clans. The Ventrue felt like they idealized Charlemange's approach to the HRE: a new monarchy that wanted to be the next Rome with powerful rulers forcing order on the serfs and peasants. The Lasombra felt like they represented the underside of courtly intrigue and the hunger for power for power's sake. The Tzimisce felt... honest. They were brutal warlords in life, and brutal warlords in death. They dispatched with the lofty airs of the Venture, and the pointless politicking of the Lasombra. The violence of Vicissitude helped reinforce that impression. They were terrifying in a visceral and direct way without any need for pretense. Only those they considered peers earned any sort of respect and formalities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T16:45:09-07:00","id":1480220,"title":"","content":"I am a huge Tzimisce fan. I think the Modern Tzimisce are barely worth their weight in blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T17:48:04-07:00","id":1480225,"title":"","content":"This is a topic that definitely has a range of opinions.<br /> <br /> One the one hand, you've got people like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> who are really into the Dark Ages depiction of the Tzimisce as Dracula-types and have an extreme dislike for the Modern Nights Tzimisce that focus predominantly on body horror and squick.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you have a lot of Tzimisce fans who consider Vicissitude the single most important and interesting aspect of the Tzimisce, and will go &quot;what's the point even?&quot; if you try and imagine the Tzimisce without it.<br /> <br /> And then you've got folks like me somewhere in the middle, who finds the body horror aspect fun and doesn't want to see it go away necessarily, but doesn't like the entire Clan being reduced to that single stereotype either, and thus tends to carry some of that Old World culture into the Modern Nights with them. Might be why I enjoy Radu's &quot;Modest Proposal&quot; to Velya the Vivisectionist so much, since it almost takes this OOC debate and turns it into an IC discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T18:10:58-07:00","id":1480227,"title":"","content":"I love the Tzimisci. I like their Dark Ages iteration, and I also like their modern iteration. They Tzimisci have changed more than any other clan over the last thousand years. The modern iteration also serves as nice counterbalance to the Lasombra. With the Lasombra, the full clan joined the Sabbat and brought all of their rituals with them. With the Tzimisci, the Old Clan didn't. So the Sabbat Tzimisci lost a chunk of their heritage and forged a new identity for themselves. <br /> <br /> I also like how the Tzimisci went from being lords in the Dark Ages to being the priests of the Sabbat. And the Lasombra went from being priests in the Dark Ages to being lords in the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T18:15:03-07:00","id":1480228,"title":"","content":"Random OOC story:<br /> <br /> <b>Mi Castle Su Castle</b><br /> <br /> My all-time favorite Tzimisce character was inspired by the song &quot;Hungry Eyes.&quot; I watched the music video of it and proceeded to make this as an NPC/PC for a short game with the premise that he was a member of the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The character, Jeffrey Jones, owned an apartment building. It was an extremely nice apartment building that was strangely cheap but in the bad part of town. It was heavily gated and had its own private security company but a very strange set of rules. Basically, you signed the contract only after extensive interviews and background checks. You also were very much at the mercy of the landowner in eviction but you had rent control and utilities covered.<br /> <br /> You lived very well if you put your life entirely in the landlord's hands, basically, and made a token offering every month.<br /> <br /> Unbeknownst to the residents, the place was heavily wired and bugged with security cameras everywhere as well as Auspex as his Primary Discipline. The owner wished to know everything about his people and used that to manipulate them. The animals in the building were all loyal to him as well, dogs, cats, and if there were rats then they always stayed out of sight. He eventually learned the Out of Clan Discipline of Presence. Dominate was too crude for him but he wished his tenants to LOVE him.<br /> <br /> Jeffrey had plans beyond ruling one apartment building, though. He eventually had the owners of the nearby grocery store murdered so he could buy out their business. From there, he set up a delivery service to his apartment building. He bought out the Chinese restaurant across the street and gave discounts to delivery to the apartment. He couldn't acquire a nearby public school but was considering getting a private school established and LOVED home schooling families.<br /> <br /> You see, the goal of Jeffrey Jones was that eventually these people would never leave his territory. They would have everything they needed provided to them and he could always know who they were, where they were, and what they did. To gather hundreds of hours of footage of them from birth until death. He fed on them, yes, and cultivated them as a herd with easy ways to access their homes (he has the keys) and knowing when they ate, slept, and defecated.<br /> <br /> No one would ever threaten them and he would protect them but they were, of course, the sweetest blood that they offered to him in tribute.<br /> <br /> Jeffrey Jones was a Tzimisce Anitribu of the Camarilla who had one simple desire: <i>to own his tenants</i>. Body and soul. That every night, he was SURROUNDED by his territory and people like a warm coffin.<br /> <br /> Other vampires...just wouldn't understand.<br /> <br /> DO NOT TRY AND MOVE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-05-2022, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:14:07-07:00","id":1480235,"title":"","content":"I find them rather frustrating, because they don't quite do their job of being playable Wamphyri. Vicissitude is too powerful in direct combat, and too weak as a prep-time-power. If you actually look at what the Wamphyri can do, they have roughly three or four dots worth of Requim Protean, and the ability to create powerful warbeasts if they have a long, long time to work in a laboratory. They have zero, absolutely zero, ability to warp other people's flesh in direct combat. Their powers are better represented by Protean and some sort of Thaumaturgy ritual that can only be used in conjunction with Protean and which requires a laboratory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:32:26-07:00","id":1480236,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Vampires+Cronenberg-y/Barker-y body horror is a solid idea combo. Not one to all tastes, sure, but there is a certain &quot;yeah, you could totally combine those things and find certain horror-y stylistic and thematic resonances in doing so&quot; vibe deep down. For all that the modern conception of the Tzimisce might feel shallow to some, there is at the heart of that an evocative concept with strong legs to stand on and spin out from. Which is probably a big ol part of why the modern iteration has the fairly vociferous fans that they do (and being real, ones who have no idea what Whampyri even are as far as what is getting a response out of them. &quot;Vampires+Body horror&quot; is an idea that can live well outside that source material). Even if it is shallow (which can be argued, I'm just saying, even if you lean that way), one of the forever strengths of VtM and part of why it hit so hard is, well, the sheer presence of its style and imagery, grotesque and otherwise. The modern Tzimisce express that, in their own way, even if it might be considered by some to be a simplistic way. They give a lot for people into that kind of thing to play around with and perhaps even find depth in, if they choose.<br /> <br /> And I say that as someone who has run yeeeeaaaaaaars of Dark Ages campaigns, so as an ST I certainly have my preferred flavour of Tzimisce as far as how I use them in my own games. I just get why the modern Tzim have spent.. what, 4 editions of present day VtM now? (they barely existed in 1e) in more or less their same shape (Vic as alien astral disease for instance didn't really change how the main body of the clan expressed themselves, it just threw in a very particular why for it). Like the Assamites, the Setites, the Ravnos, any number of clans have had comparatively huge shifts in attempted approach (or attempted blowing them up no less) up and down the line. The modern Tzim continued to trade just fine in the material as &quot;them monstrous body horror vampires&quot; and still be clamoured for. They're bizarre and grotesque and frankly some edgelord-y stuff, and yet also accessibly and comprehensibly so. It's worth considering thus that there's something to that on a level of gaming craft. It might not thrill you, but truly, there's so much worse things out there as far as gaming things people like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  grammar 05-05-2022, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:50:43-07:00","id":1480239,"title":"","content":"Well, I\u2019ll add my voice to those who love Old Clan Tzimisce but aren\u2019t particularly interested in the newer Clan. I love the ultra-traditional, territorial, honorable yet cruel elders of the Clan and would want to use them in a modern game as well. The sadistic body horror stuff doesn\u2019t do it for me, in fact some of the material on them almost seemed to fetishize torture, which was a bit creepy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480228#post1480228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeffrey Jones was a Tzimisce Anitribu of the Camarilla who had one simple desire: <i>to own his tenants</i>. Body and soul. That every night, he was SURROUNDED by his territory and people like a warm coffin.<br /> <br /> Other vampires...just wouldn't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this character concept and have long wanted the Tzimisce to be in the Camarilla. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:51:25-07:00","id":1480240,"title":"","content":"(It feels like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477124-clan-tzimisce-is-the-least-interesting-clan#post1477124\">we just did this</a> .... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> They were my favorite clan for a while, especially back in the early days of Vampire: The Dark Ages (@1996 - 1999). I do think Vicissitude is sometimes - even often - over-played, but I've honestly found that to be true for all of the &quot;Special Sauce&quot; Disciplines (Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, Quietus, etc.). <br /> As I've mentioned elsewhere, I prefer drawing more on some of the Eastern European cultural influences, including how they sometimes map to other places, as well as a lot of the more mystical trans humanism/trans-vampirism from Requiem's Ordo Dracul book, and certain aspects of urban xenophobia/cliquishness/isolationism. And I've always just liked Dracula. (I like Frankenstein and the Wolfman <i>more</i>, but Dracula is still cool.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T19:53:30-07:00","id":1480241,"title":"","content":"They fill their intended niche. Otherworldly evil, body horror and twisted visionaries. I don\u2019t understand why people who wish Tzimisce were more like Ventrue and Tremere didn\u2019t just roll Ventrue or Tremere. It\u2019s okay to not like the clan. Why waste the efforts trying to reinvent them to be something you like, especially when they already have an established, 30-year-strong fan base? Just seems weird, like wishing Gangrel weren\u2019t so wild, and maybe did art instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:02:32-07:00","id":1480243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480239#post1480239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this character concept and have long wanted the Tzimisce to be in the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise to both. <br /> <br /> (At some point about 15+ years ago, I just decided that everyone was a member of the Camarilla - and the Anarchs, really - and the Sabbat were a bunch of cults who were much more focused on their Paths than they were on Clans.)<br /> <br /> And yes, in hindsight, I think Rob Hatch had a bit too much of a fixation on the torture aspect. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480241#post1480241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just seems weird, like wishing Gangrel weren\u2019t so wild, and maybe did art instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once knew a guy who did wood carving with chainsaws. I always thought it would make an interesting aspect to a Gangrel character. (Said guy also looked like Grizzly Adams, owned a pair of wolf-dogs, and a giant tarantula.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:06:57-07:00","id":1480244,"title":"","content":"Is this a bait thread?<br /> <br /> If its not, guess I'll answer seriously.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are interesting because of their body horror motif and mechanics, point blank. They were an inversion of the typical unvaried, unexciting of the &quot;Dracula&quot; trope. They used to exemplify the inherent strangeness of vampirism at their basest facet. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points out, they were brutal warlords of the land, who had their subjects, whether human or else, as their own play-doh playthings. They didn't need &quot;favors&quot; as masters of their own realms. Many other clans needed favors from <i>them</i>. And if you think body or eldritch-influenced horror don't make for compelling stories, I guess you never read stuff from H.P Lovecraft or the numerous others that have been inspired by his work before.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce in their clanbooks (from what I remember from reading them long ago) were great exploration pieces on body horror, especially the Paths they used to have (RIP Paths) to go with characters you made from their clan.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce Antediluvian [Tzimisce] was also one of the most badass Antediluvians there was. Without Vicissitude, half the feats [Tzimisce] did throughout VTM franchise wouldn't have been possible.<br /> <br /> But alas, the Tzimisce are basically milquetoast as of now. The current writers basically (essentially) divorced them from the Sabbat and made them Anarch-aligned when they never were, and also made them into a cheesy &quot;lol hoarders dragon dracula modern-day landlord trope&quot; now. Also with the new &quot;morality system&quot; (the Twilight Saga system, as I personally dub it), Tzimisce now must have Touchstones.. which is character breaking because Tzimisce are one of the clans who historically NEVER cared about abiding by humanity or seeing a single human as being more important than themselves (because Touchstones force you to be a superpowered babysitter and a low-hanging fruit for the ST to make contrived drama, by making scenarios in which the Touchstone gets arbitrarily put in danger.. but usually, from what I hear from instances in which V5 is played, Touchstones are just literally forgotten most of the time. lol).<br /> <br /> Not only that, Vicissitude doesn't even exist anymore in V5. Its been rolled into Protean (which basically means it doesn't really exist). That's why I even first tacked this thread as a bait thread, because the ideology you have towards Vicissitude is one shared by the new writers of VTM, thus Vicissitude being already removed.. why complain about something that doesn't exist for a clan anymore?<br /> <br /> Not only that, the type of Tzimisce you talk about are literally already a clan variant already (Kolduns, pre-V5). Even then, Kolduns can and do use Vicissitude. As a matter-of-fact, I don't even think Kolduns are a thing in V5 anymore and I don't even think Koldunic Sorcery even exists in V5 either (as in, varied different forms of Blood Sorcery. Dynamicism and Diversity in Disciplines shafted for formulaic &quot;streamlining&quot;).<br /> <br /> Hell, Tzimisce don't even have Auspex anymore; which to many other pre-V5 Tzimisce fans, was integral to the function of letting the Tzimisce being ultimate purveyors of their land, along with being scholar-seer-warlords. Now it got replaced with... Dominate? Such a replacement clues to the fact whoever made the change, did not understand the Tzimisce (something other posters in other threads on this topic have pointed out).<br /> <br /> So 2/3rds (Auspex and Koldunic Sorcery) of the thing you like about the Tzimisce don't even exist for them now, unless you were inferring this thread, as a V20 thread? If not this being specifically a thread about V20 and before, why complain about Vicissitude when it doesn't exist in a true non-pseudo form as it does now?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it make sense to complain that Blood Sorcery diversity is gone and that Auspex was removed from the Tzimisce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 05-05-2022, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:12:39-07:00","id":1480245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480243#post1480243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likewise to both.<br /> <br /> (At some point about 15+ years ago, I just decided that everyone was a member of the Camarilla - and the Anarchs, really - and the Sabbat were a bunch of cults who were much more focused on their Paths than they were on Clans.)<br /> <br /> And yes, in hindsight, I think Rob Hatch had a bit too much of a fixation on the torture aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve done something similar, with most Clans as members of the Camarilla and the Anarchs existing mostly within the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> I also have a version of the Sabbat as being almost entirely Clanless. This Sabbat rejects the idea of Clans as being inherently divisive in keeping young vampires from uniting against the elders and even as the taint of the Antediluvians. With rare exceptions, almost all Sabbat vampires who belong to a Clan are elders were were around during the Anarch Revolts and even they don\u2019t acknowledge their Clan or organize based on it. For centuries, almost every Sabbat vampire has been embraced through the mixing of blood, leading to Caitiff or, in some cases, unusual bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:29:22-07:00","id":1480248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480244#post1480244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a bait thread?<br /> <br /> If its not, guess I'll answer seriously.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce are interesting because of their body horror motif and mechanics, point blank. They were an inversion of the typical unvaried, unexciting of the &quot;Dracula&quot; trope. They used to exemplify the inherent strangeness of vampirism at their basest facet. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points out, they were brutal warlords of the land, who had their subjects, whether human or else, as their own play-doh playthings. They didn't need &quot;favors&quot; as masters of their own realms. Many other clans needed favors from <i>them</i>. And if you think body or eldritch-influenced horror don't make for compelling stories, I guess you never read stuff from H.P Lovecraft or the numerous others that have been inspired by his work before.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually pretty much the nail on the head why the Tzimisce have always been a square peg in a round hole. Because they're not alien and can never be alien. Vampire: The Masquerade is intensely mono-focused on GOTHIC horror while HP Lovecraft is about COSMIC horror. The two can be combined as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> can and has done but the important thing to remember is that the vampires are never the alien ones.<br /> <br /> V:TM is a game intensely monofocused on sin, damnation, remorse, guilt, and losing your humanity. Even the Sabbat and the other &quot;evil&quot; vampires are all about rejecting their humanity but ultimately, their morality is intensely IMPORTANT and so is their status as damned monsters. Which is absolutely impossible in cosmic horror. The game makes it clear that even Path followers never actually successfully become truly alien, they just reject it.<br /> <br /> And why would the Tzimisce be particularly alien versus any other vampire?<br /> <br /> It isn't exactly an interesting character type either. &quot;My character doesn't have comprehensible motives&quot; isn't a good roleplaying opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:31:35-07:00","id":1480249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480244#post1480244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, Tzimisce don't even have Auspex anymore; which to many other pre-V5 Tzimisce fans, was integral to the function of letting the Tzimisce being ultimate purveyors of their land, along with being scholar-seer-warlords. Now it got replaced with... Dominate? Such a replacement clues to the fact whoever made the change, did not understand the Tzimisce (something other posters in other threads on this topic have pointed out).<br /> <br /> So 2/3rds (Auspex and Koldunic Sorcery) of the thing you like about the Tzimisce don't even exist for them now, unless you were inferring this thread, as a V20 thread? If not this being specifically a thread about V20 and before, why complain about Vicissitude when it doesn't exist in a true non-pseudo form as it does now?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it make sense to complain that Blood Sorcery diversity is gone and that Auspex was removed from the Tzimisce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex was also crucial to the idea that Tzims rule by cruelly punishing thought-crime rather than hypnotizing people into doing things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T20:55:39-07:00","id":1480253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480249#post1480249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex was also crucial to the idea that Tzims rule by cruelly punishing thought-crime rather than hypnotizing people into doing things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex and Animalism are also somewhat useful for doing a lot of classic witchcraft/pagan mysticism tropes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T21:02:39-07:00","id":1480254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually pretty much the nail on the head why the Tzimisce have always been a square peg in a round hole. Because they're not alien and can never be alien. Vampire: The Masquerade is intensely mono-focused on GOTHIC horror while HP Lovecraft is about COSMIC horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess with this logic, the various other clans that were divorced from being solely gothic horror, are &quot;squares&quot; as well.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel are a focus on bestial-primordial horror, along with inherent inhuman savagery. They're about the wilds of things and the things that lurk in the darkness of the woods.<br /> <br /> The Brujah represent rage on levels humans can hardly understand. One moment you're having a deep thought-provoking philosophical conversation with a strangely charming person, but one wrong misplaced word, then you'll have your throat ripped out; but you're still semi-conscious, because of the way on how fast it was ripped out to begin with. The last thing you would see is that formerly charming man holding up your head and staring you at you with glowing red eyes. The Bruaj<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set were about occultic horror. About how far you could be pulled in, deeper and deeper, into a group that seemed innocuous on the surface, but as much darker secrets. As you learn the secrets of the group further on, you get tied in deeper; even if you wanted to leave, THEY won't let you and you have to do their bidding. You'd see things that would change you forever, things you'll get to never take back seeing.<br /> <br /> I can go on about other clans, but the bottomline of what I'm saying to say, is that VTM is more than &quot;gothic horror&quot;. And to say Vampires aren't inherently alien doesn't make sense. They are, by virtue of being non-human and completely different from everything a human is. Other Vampires once changed to being an alien from their own former species, coped in trying to cling onto Humanity. The Tzimisce were different and were interesting because they embraced their inherent inhumaneness. They don't behold themselves to the norms of human society, which is why they were one of the pillars of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Paths allowed you to greater roleplay into being a Vampire and how they would make philosophies complete divorced from regular human understanding. That's what made the Tzimisce being one of the templars of being a Vampire in VTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T21:04:20-07:00","id":1480255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480254#post1480254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I guess with this logic, the various other clans that were divorced from being solely gothic horror, are &quot;squares&quot; as well.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel are a focus on bestial-primordial horror, along with inherent inhuman savagery. They're about the wilds of things and the things that lurk in the darkness of the woods.<br /> <br /> The Brujah represent rage on levels humans can hardly understand. One moment you're having a deep thought-provoking philosophical conversation with a strangely charming person, but one wrong misplaced word, then you'll have your throat ripped out; but you're still semi-conscious, because of the way on how fast it was ripped out to begin with. The last thing you would see is that formerly charming man holding up your head and staring you at you with glowing red eyes. The Bruaj<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set were about occultic horror. About how far you could be pulled in, deeper and deeper, into a group that seemed innocuous on the surface, but as much darker secrets. As you learn the secrets of the group further on, you get tied in deeper; even if you wanted to leave, THEY won't let you and you have to do their bidding. You'd see things that would change you forever, things you'll get to never take back seeing.<br /> <br /> I can go on about other clans, but the bottomline of what I'm saying to say, is that VTM is more than &quot;gothic horror&quot;. And to say Vampires aren't inherently alien doesn't make sense. They are, by virtue of being non-human and completely different from everything a human is. Other Vampires once changed to being an alien from their own former species, coped in trying to cling onto humanity. The Tzimisce were different and were interesting because they embraced their inherent inhumaneness. They don't behold themselves to the norms of human society, which is why they were one of the pillars of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Paths allowed you to greater roleplay into being a Vampire and how they would make philosophies complete divorced from regular human understanding. That's what made the Tzimisce being one of the templars of being a Vampire in VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all of them are very good for Gothic horror.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose Gothic PUNK.<br /> <br /> Which alienness doesn't do well for either.<br /> <br /> But that's my thoughts, YMMV.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T02:10:32-07:00","id":1480275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480241#post1480241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They fill their intended niche. Otherworldly evil, body horror and twisted visionaries. I don\u2019t understand why people who wish Tzimisce were more like Ventrue and Tremere didn\u2019t just roll Ventrue or Tremere. It\u2019s okay to not like the clan. Why waste the efforts trying to reinvent them to be something you like, especially when they already have an established, 30-year-strong fan base? Just seems weird, like wishing Gangrel weren\u2019t so wild, and maybe did art instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts on the matter, succinctly and persuasively expressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T10:54:31-07:00","id":1480298,"title":"","content":"It's more, I suppose:<br /> <br /> 1. Why are Tzimisce &quot;alien&quot; versus any other clan? If souleaters are silly, and they are, what makes them different?<br /> <br /> 2. Doesn't making them alien make them impossible to get deep into roleplaying?<br /> <br /> 3. Why are they more EVIL than other Clans? What is so weird about them? Is it just &quot;fleshcrafting is gross&quot;?<br /> <br /> 4. Why can't fleshcrafting be used for healing or non-evil uses? What about a Tzimisce plastic or trauma surgeon?<br /> <br /> 5. What motivtes an &quot;alien&quot; mindset versus the traditional Beast, Hunger, power, and guilt/old self?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T11:28:21-07:00","id":1480301,"title":"","content":"One part I always enjoyed was the clan weakness tying them to a certain place, as it allowed for a lot of that &quot;The Land and The King Are One&quot; sort of thing as well as (seeing how these are vampires) the trope of pieces of land being &quot;sour&quot; or corrupted (ala Stephen King's Pet Semitary , etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T13:00:38-07:00","id":1480304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Why are Tzimisce &quot;alien&quot; versus any other clan? If souleaters are silly, and they are, what makes them different?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because out of all the clans, the Tzimisce embraced their vampiric nature almost more than anyone else. They are one the most disaffected from the tedious qualms of humanity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Doesn't making them alien make them impossible to get deep into roleplaying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many people who played pre-V5 Tzimisce have done so in the past, why infer its &quot;impossible&quot;? Good or semi-decent roleplayers would get by readily and without any trouble playing a Tzismice. Even besides that, what you ask depends completely on who's playing that specific character in question. Some can play as a Toreador for instance, one of the clans more inclined toward being human than alien, but mess up roleplaying them completely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Why are they more EVIL than other Clans? What is so weird about them? Is it just &quot;fleshcrafting is gross&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tzimisce as a clan as whole, have done numerous objectively evil things during the course of game. Saying they're more evil though, than the other clans? I don't know for sure about that admittedly. <br /> <br /> The weirdness? The weirdness of the Tzimisce speaks for itself and fleshcrafting is large component of that, but the Tzimisce have many other things going for them that make them <i>very</i> weird. But again, like the evil thing, I wouldn't say they're the most weird of vampiredom. That'd have to go to the Kisayd and the even lesser known Kisayd bloodline (who I forgot the name of).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Why can't fleshcrafting be used for healing or non-evil uses? What about a Tzimisce plastic or trauma surgeon?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've ever read the Tzimisce clanbook before, you should know that what you ask for, literally already was a sample character concept for a Tzimisce before. Tzimisce surgeon. I haven't read the Tzimisce clanbook in years, but even I still remember that sample character. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. What motivtes an &quot;alien&quot; mindset versus the traditional Beast, Hunger, power, and guilt/old self?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paths (specifically, Path of Metamorphosis).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T13:13:36-07:00","id":1480305,"title":"","content":"As much as I love the Tzimisce, A LOT of vampire clans have &quot;fully embrace their vampirism&quot; as a thing.<br /> <br /> * Followers of Set<br /> * Baali<br /> * Lasombra<br /> * Gangrel<br /> <br /> I mean, aside from the Salubri, who DOESNT embrace their vampirism?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T13:58:37-07:00","id":1480309,"title":"","content":"I don't dislike the Tzismce clan, but there extreme alien mindset and clan weakness made it hard for me to use in a game. Personally I have a soft spot for the Old Clan branch as fearsome lore collectors and problematic protectors of there domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T15:04:12-07:00","id":1480312,"title":"","content":"I admittedly haven't read the original Tzimisce Clanbook (yet), so maybe it goes more into this idea, but &quot;alien&quot; has never been the way I have viewed the Tzimisce mindset, because Alien is fundamentally Other, whereas a Vampire is only somewhat Other. I went over this a bit in one of the previous topics discussing the Tzimisce, but while they may lean more into their vampiric nature than most, they remain intrinsically tied to their origin as a human being; that influence may fade over time, but less so if they have to continue mingling with humanity in order to meet their needs and hold on to power, and it will continue to have an influence on their trajectory even when their mortal days become a fraction of the time they have endured compared to their vampire nights. The idea that the pre-Embrace identity of a Tzimisce has no influence over them post-Embrace is one of the greatest flaws of their Clan culture in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I do think there is a significant difference between the approach of the Tzimisce, who embrace their vampirism in a more comprehensive and philosophical way, than other examples like the Gangrel, who embrace the more animalistic and predatory parts of their vampiric nature, or the Lasombra, who embrace the more authoritarian and predatory parts of their vampiric nature. They embrace particular aspects, while what makes the Tzimisce distinct is their attempt to really explore the fundamental nature of their condition, and then try and surpass its limitations. But I still don't consider that to be fundamentally Alien, because vampires do not come from a fundamentally different world compared to humanity. Maybe if you had something like the Soul-Eaters, something from an entirely different reality, influencing them, but just being vampires doesn't make them completely Other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T15:31:01-07:00","id":1480316,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m trying to decide if I should just make the \u201cOld Clan\u201d (who VDA20 dubs the \u201cDracul\u201d) the Tzimisce Antitribu in the Camarilla to play them up more in the setting.<br /> <br /> edit: I think the main argument against it is that they\u2019d never align themselves with the Tremere, so by that argument they should either be independent holding their Eastern European territory and treating with other vampires on a case by case basis, or of course use the Tal\u2019mahe\u2019Ra","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-07-2022, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:09:34-07:00","id":1480375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480298#post1480298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Why are Tzimisce &quot;alien&quot; versus any other clan? If souleaters are silly, and they are, what makes them different?<br /> <br /> 2. Doesn't making them alien make them impossible to get deep into roleplaying?<br /> <br /> 3. Why are they more EVIL than other Clans? What is so weird about them? Is it just &quot;fleshcrafting is gross&quot;?<br /> <br /> 4. Why can't fleshcrafting be used for healing or non-evil uses? What about a Tzimisce plastic or trauma surgeon?<br /> <br /> 5. What motivtes an &quot;alien&quot; mindset versus the traditional Beast, Hunger, power, and guilt/old self?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Why are fomori &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; versus any other human? If Banes are silly, and they are, what makes fomori different from humans?<br /> <br /> 2. Doesn't making fomori &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; make it impossible to get deep into roleplaying?<br /> <br /> 3. Why are fomori more EVIL than other humans? What is so weird about them? Is it just &quot;Wyrm corruption is gross&quot;?<br /> <br /> 4. Why can't Wyrm corruption be used for healing or non-evil uses? What about a fomor plastic or trauma surgeon?<br /> <br /> 5. What motivates a &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; mindset versus the traditional Glory, Honor, Wisdom, and protecting Gaia?<br /> <br /> Don't take it too seriously; the above is just how your questions come across to me. I continue to find it hard understand why some people seem to think that the concept of otherworldly corruption is totally kosher is one game line set in the World of Darkness, but completely beyond the pale in a related game line also set in the World of Darkness. Given that the Sabbat, the Tzimisce, Vicissitude, and Souleaters were all written by the very same person who also wrote <i>Freak Legion: A Players Guide to Fomori,</i> it seems painfully obvious to me that Souleaters and Banes describe the same entities or phenomenon from different points of view, and pretty much the only real difference is the terminology used. If one is silly, so is the other; if one is not silly, neither is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:16:32-07:00","id":1480376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480375#post1480375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Why are fomori &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; versus any other human? If Banes are silly, and they are, what makes fomori different from humans?<br /> <br /> 2. Doesn't making fomori &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; make it impossible to get deep into roleplaying?<br /> <br /> 3. Why are fomori more EVIL than other humans? What is so weird about them? Is it just &quot;Wyrm corruption is gross&quot;?<br /> <br /> 4. Why can't Wyrm corruption be used for healing or non-evil uses? What about a fomor plastic or trauma surgeon?<br /> <br /> 5. What motivates a &quot;Wyrm corrupted&quot; mindset versus the traditional Glory, Honor, Wisdom, and protecting Gaia?<br /> <br /> Don't take it too seriously; the above is just how your questions come across to me. I continue to find it hard understand why some people seem to think that the concept of otherworldly corruption is totally kosher is one game line set in the World of Darkness, but completely beyond the pale in a related game line also set in the World of Darkness. Given that the Sabbat, the Tzimisce, Vicissitude, and Souleaters were all written by the very same person who also wrote <i>Freak Legion: A Players Guide to Fomori,</i> it seems painfully obvious to me that Souleaters and Banes describe the same entities or phenomenon from different points of view, and pretty much the only real difference is the terminology used. If one is silly, so is the other; if one is not silly, neither is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, absolutely. Formori don't have free will so they are impossible to roleplay.<br /> <br /> I don't think they can be a meaningful story told about them.<br /> <br /> It's like roleplaying a Dalek.<br /> <br /> Don't you agree that a creature without free will is just an NPC? They're effectively like roleplaying a hammer or a car. The Wyrm uses them. They're not characters.<br /> <br /> They exist for Garou to slaughter because any salvation or choice to be other than a tool is impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:18:34-07:00","id":1480377,"title":"","content":"Anyway, &quot;alien&quot; in the WOD is generally just a way of saying &quot;without empathy&quot;, empathy being considered the defining trait of humanity. The Tzims are notorious for being even more lacking in empathy than other vampires, and they have H.R. Giger artistic tastes. Their powers tend to erode humanity even faster than most, because you really need to just view humans as building material if you are turning them into vozhds. Hence, Tzims are even more likely to follow Roads/Paths than other vampires. So they lack empathy, so they are, as the WOD defines such things, alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:20:52-07:00","id":1480378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480376#post1480376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, yes, absolutely. Formori don't have free will so they are impossible to roleplay.<br /> <br /> I don't think they can be a meaningful story told about them.<br /> <br /> It's like roleplaying a Dalek.<br /> <br /> Don't you agree that a creature without free will is just an NPC? They're effectively like roleplaying a hammer or a car. The Wyrm uses them. They're not characters.<br /> <br /> They exist for Garou to slaughter because any salvation or choice to be other than a tool is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has them lacking free will been consistently established? Because I don't remember that being a thing in Freak Legon....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T11:21:30-07:00","id":1480379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480377#post1480377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, &quot;alien&quot; in the WOD is generally just a way of saying &quot;without empathy&quot;, empathy being considered the defining trait of humanity. The Tzims are notorious for being even more lacking in empathy than other vampires, and they have H.R. Giger artistic tastes. Their powers tend to erode humanity even faster than most, because you really need to just view humans as building material if you are turning them into vozhds. Hence, Tzims are even more likely to follow Roads/Paths than other vampires. So they lack empathy, so they are, as the WOD defines such things, alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's not reflected in the rules with the fact that they have less Conscience. It also feels like something that blaming their powers for is a weird choice. Because, yes, making vozhds is horrible but Vicissitude would be fantastically useful for a High Humanity vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T12:48:21-07:00","id":1480387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480379#post1480379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, that's not reflected in the rules with the fact that they have less Conscience. It also feels like something that blaming their powers for is a weird choice. Because, yes, making vozhds is horrible but Vicissitude would be fantastically useful for a High Humanity vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>At some point I would like to try playing a Dark Ages Tzimisce on the Road of Heaven who has set themselves up as a sort of &quot;false saint&quot; miracle worker and attracted a cult following by healing injuries and deformities. All of this done with the best of intentions, but the adage about the road to hell and all that does exist for a reason.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I think you could do a really interesting DA character on the Road of Humanity who is a natural philosopher and maybe graduate from the medical school in Salerno who is just really fixated on being a better healer, using the lower levels of Vicissitude for both surgery and anatomical study.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised you never really saw it being used for espionage and infiltration. Being able to alter your features combined with Auspex and Animalism seems like a useful skillset for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Added: I also think it would be somewhat amusing to play a modern Tzimisce who is extremely vain and has used Vicissitude to obtain extraordinary physical beauty, but has it at level 4 so they also have the horrid form thing going (maybe a reflection of what a shallow and terrible person they really are, sort of like Dorian Gray's painting). Effectively Beauty and The Beast at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-07-2022, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T12:58:43-07:00","id":1480390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480312#post1480312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think there is a significant difference between the approach of the Tzimisce, who embrace their vampirism in a more comprehensive and philosophical way, than other examples like the Gangrel, who embrace the more animalistic and predatory parts of their vampiric nature, or the Lasombra, who embrace the more authoritarian and predatory parts of their vampiric nature. They embrace particular aspects, while what makes the Tzimisce distinct is their attempt to really explore the fundamental nature of their condition, and then try and surpass its limitations. But I still don't consider that to be fundamentally Alien, because vampires do not come from a fundamentally different world compared to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is close to the approach I take in my chronicles. I simply don't like Necroscope and find their version of vampires incompatible to traditional kinds. So I removed the Vicissitude Discipline in my game and gave the Tzimisce Protean instead. I still wanted to depict the Tzimisce close to what they are in canon, but obviously Vicissitude is so deeply mixed with the clan's culture I had to do a lot of surgery. <br /> <br /> One of my solutions is that the Tzimisce see vampires as a completely different than humanity. They aren't humans with a disease or curse. The blood makes them something else, similar to how an insect shifts between its instars. But humans can't do that unless Vitae is involved. So I made that kind of belief in metamorphosis important to the clan and basis for the Path of the same name, but focusing more on the essence of Vitae and its effects and what it means rather than the use of Vicissitude. Less body horror, but more emphasis on truly alien mindset from humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:00:00-07:00","id":1480391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480387#post1480387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point I would like to try playing a Dark Ages Tzimisce on the Road of Heaven who has set themselves up as a sort of &quot;false saint&quot; miracle worker and attracted a cult following by healing injuries and deformities. All of this done with the best of intentions, but the adage about the road to hell and all that does exist for a reason.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I think you could do a really interesting DA character on the Road of Humanity who is a natural philosopher and maybe graduate from the medical school in Salerno who is just really fixated on being a better healer, using the lower levels of Vicissitude for both surgery and anatomical study.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised you never really saw it being used for espionage and infiltration. Being able to alter your features combined with Auspex and Animalism seems like a useful skillset for that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had an idea for a Tzimisce anthropologist that would use Vicissitude to live among different human populations as if they were one of them in order to study them, even mimicking aging over time in order to blend in, until they eventually left when it came time to fake their death, only to come back with a new persona or find a different population to study if they were finished with that group. Still a little detached, but way more empathetic than the typical Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:05:18-07:00","id":1480392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480391#post1480391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had an idea for a Tzimisce anthropologist that would use Vicissitude to live among different human populations as if they were one of them in order to study them, even mimicking aging over time in order to blend in, until they eventually left when it came time to fake their death, only to come back with a new persona or find a different population to study if they were finished with that group. Still a little detached, but way more empathetic than the typical Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I could really see one of the Oburtus doing that. Not sure why, but it just seems suitable.<br /> <br /> I also like how that idea takes the whole &quot;I am the lord and these are my serfs&quot; trope mentality and recasts it in an interesting new form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:05:22-07:00","id":1480393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480376#post1480376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yes, absolutely. Formori don't have free will so they are impossible to roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not my view of fomori, but then again I dislike much of the presentation about the Wyrm in Werewolf. To me, &quot;fomori&quot; as a concept simply covers a way to simulate all those monsters in legend, folklore, and pop culture of things that were once human or animal, but now clearly have supernatural powers. That ranges from anything from the Erymanthean Boar and harpies of Greek legend to Lovecraft's Deep Ones and ghouls.<br /> <br /> Sure there is a Bane possessing them, but how different is that than a vampire with a Beast?<br /> <br /> It's totally fine to interpret fomori differently, or not find the canonical fomori in Werewolf to be compelling. But the generic concept itself can be used in lots of different ways that don't deviate much from as it is written.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:12:08-07:00","id":1480394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480375#post1480375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems painfully obvious to me that Souleaters and Banes describe the same entities or phenomenon from different points of view, and pretty much the only real difference is the terminology used.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree. As originally described, they seem very much like fomori except without using the mechanics of Werewolf. <br /> <br /> While I don't like Vicissitude because I find Necroscope style vampires to be completely different and inconsistent from the vampires of the gothic tradition and the stated Gothic Punk nature of the game, I actually have no problem with them being some strange abomination for Garou to destroy. So while divorcing the Tzimisce from that plot, I basically took the Souleaters as originally described in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and use them on occasion as a fomori in Werewolf. Of course, rather than use the story of Andeleon, I make it more like Invasion of the Body Snatchers and lift more from Necroscope as &quot;invaders from the deep umbra&quot; instead of &quot;vampires with really strange discipline&quot;. There's just a lot less Souleaters out there than Sabbat Tzimisce.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:14:02-07:00","id":1480395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480390#post1480390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is close to the approach I take in my chronicles. I simply don't like Necroscope and find their version of vampires incompatible to traditional kinds. So I removed the Vicissitude Discipline in my game and gave the Tzimisce Protean instead. I still wanted to depict the Tzimisce close to what they are in canon, but obviously Vicissitude is so deeply mixed with the clan's culture I had to do a lot of surgery.<br /> <br /> One of my solutions is that the Tzimisce see vampires as a completely different than humanity. They aren't humans with a disease or curse. The blood makes them something else, similar to how an insect shifts between its instars. But humans can't do that unless Vitae is involved. So I made that kind of belief in metamorphosis important to the clan and basis for the Path of the same name, but focusing more on the essence of Vitae and its effects and what it means rather than the use of Vicissitude. Less body horror, but more emphasis on truly alien mindset from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall some of the better material about the clan and the path taking that route. I may be Mandella Effecting that with the Ordo Dracul though.<br /> <br /> As for giving them Protean, one could in theory work up alloyed discipline powers/devotions that combine Protean with maybe Potence or Fortitude (or even Dominate) to do some of the fleshcrafting effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:14:18-07:00","id":1480396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480393#post1480393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not my view of fomori, but then again I dislike much of the presentation about the Wyrm in Werewolf. To me, &quot;fomori&quot; as a concept simply covers a way to simulate all those monsters in legend, folklore, and pop culture of things that were once human or animal, but now clearly have supernatural powers. That ranges from anything from the Erymanthean Boar and harpies of Greek legend to Lovecraft's Deep Ones and ghouls.<br /> <br /> Sure there is a Bane possessing them, but how different is that than a vampire with a Beast?<br /> <br /> It's totally fine to interpret fomori differently, or not find the canonical fomori in Werewolf to be compelling. But the generic concept itself can be used in lots of different ways that don't deviate much from as it is written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, Werewolf is not my favorite game so I could be interpreting it wrong but I definitely put Formori in the vein of &quot;soulless cannon fodder for the werewolves to tear through.&quot; They're like Buffyverse vampires or monsters.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if I was a writer on Werewolf, I'd make the Werewolves more prone to being criticized (it's already halfway to the Sabbat) and monsters more ambiguous.<br /> <br /> But that's not what I got from canon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:22:17-07:00","id":1480397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480387#post1480387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point I would like to try playing a Dark Ages Tzimisce on the Road of Heaven who has set themselves up as a sort of &quot;false saint&quot; miracle worker and attracted a cult following by healing injuries and deformities. All of this done with the best of intentions, but the adage about the road to hell and all that does exist for a reason.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I think you could do a really interesting DA character on the Road of Humanity who is a natural philosopher and maybe graduate from the medical school in Salerno who is just really fixated on being a better healer, using the lower levels of Vicissitude for both surgery and anatomical study.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised you never really saw it being used for espionage and infiltration. Being able to alter your features combined with Auspex and Animalism seems like a useful skillset for that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Added: I also think it would be somewhat amusing to play a modern Tzimisce who is extremely vain and has used Vicissitude to obtain extraordinary physical beauty, but has it at level 4 so they also have the horrid form thing going (maybe a reflection of what a shallow and terrible person they really are, sort of like Dorian Gray's painting). Effectively Beauty and The Beast at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, experimenting with the Tzimisce would probably remove some of my issues if they would stop trying to make them WEIRD AND CREEPY as if that was the only way to do them.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Tzimisce Antitribu Plastic Surgeon</b>: You have the job of making people beautiful and you are supported by the Toreador. You also have been known to help some vampires live their best unlives, escape enemies, and protect the Masquerade. You have to keep yourself secret, though, because you fear the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Tzimisce Autarkis Faith Healer</b>: Missing limbs, cancer, or internal injuries? No problem. You are the person who can cure the incurable. Maybe people believe you're a miracle worker or maybe you claim to be a psychic surgeon or an alien. Doesn't matter. However, what you do is HIGHLY Masquerade breaking.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Tzimisce Antitribu Vigilante</b>: You are the night, you are BATMAN. Well not quite but you do in fact prowl the city streets of YOUR domain and feed upon the guilty. You are connected to it in a spiritual way and protecting its citizens for their blood is the bond you share with it. Maybe your definition is to punish the evil doer--or maybe your definition of &quot;evil&quot; is not so great.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Tzimisce Anarch Crimelord</b>: You have your eyes in the rats and birds of the air. You see wherever there's problems. You also can inflict horrifying punishments on anyone you are displeased with. Yes, you are the master of the city's underground. The Prince may rule the vampires of the city but you have your own kingdom.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Tzimisce Anarch Urban Druid</b>: The Werewolves claim vampires have no connection with the land. You prove them wrong. You speak to the spirits of the land and while only the ones of blood and rage will work with you willingly, it's not like they aren't any more natural than anything else. The cirty is your domain and it is your place to do its bidding as it does yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:24:26-07:00","id":1480398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480376#post1480376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, yes, absolutely. Formori don't have free will so they are impossible to roleplay.<br /> <br /> I don't think they can be a meaningful story told about them.<br /> <br /> It's like roleplaying a Dalek.<br /> <br /> Don't you agree that a creature without free will is just an NPC? They're effectively like roleplaying a hammer or a car. The Wyrm uses them. They're not characters.<br /> <br /> They exist for Garou to slaughter because any salvation or choice to be other than a tool is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably don't want to engage a hard determinist on the topic of free will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think you or I have anything like the libertarian free will that most people mean when they talk about free will, so the question is pretty meaningless to me. Also, as was pointed out above, <i>Freak Legion</i> (which I seem to remember you were fond of) certainly assumes that fomori are playable.<br /> <br /> I'm just curious why you continue to insist that Souleaters are silly but Banes are (presumably?) fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:33:37-07:00","id":1480399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480235#post1480235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find them rather frustrating, because they don't quite do their job of being playable Wamphyri. Vicissitude is too powerful in direct combat, and too weak as a prep-time-power. If you actually look at what the Wamphyri can do, they have roughly three or four dots worth of Requim Protean, and the ability to create powerful warbeasts if they have a long, long time to work in a laboratory. They have zero, absolutely zero, ability to warp other people's flesh in direct combat. Their powers are better represented by Protean and some sort of Thaumaturgy ritual that can only be used in conjunction with Protean and which requires a laboratory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may like biothaumathurgy from dirty secrets of the black hand then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:56:20-07:00","id":1480402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480396#post1480396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I admit, Werewolf is not my favorite game so I could be interpreting it wrong but I definitely put Formori in the vein of &quot;soulless cannon fodder for the werewolves to tear through.&quot; They're like Buffyverse vampires or monsters</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It sort of depends. The Possessed book for Year of the Damned had rules for Autonomy, how much free will a host still had from their Bane (or its Weaver or Wyld counterpart), including the suggestion of doing something similar to Wraith's Shadowguiding when running Possessed characters in a game. Generally, the more powerful a Fomori is, the less Autonomy it likely has, but that may not always be true. You can also give up Autonomy to get rid of deformities, so you could have a low to mid powered Fomori who looks totally human but is all but lost to the Wyrm or a hideous monstrosity that is still human inside and would desperately like to be cured. This plays in to one of the Children of Gaia tribe's schticks about believing they should try to save and cure/heal (physically, mentally, and spiritually) Fomori whenever possible instead of simply killing them. While you undoubtedly have a lot of Fomori who are eager volunteers for Pentex supersoldier programs, members of corrupt cults, and general reprobates, you also have no small amount of poor schlubs who are victims of bad luck, accidents, or just an uncaring world. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is entirely feasible for a werewolf pack to come across The Toxic Avenger, an accidentally created Fomori set on being a vigilante against Pentex and street crime, who could be a potential ally but who is almost certain to come to a tragic end. Likewise, it is entirely possible to have an all Fomori game that draws on things like Fight Club, Venom, Upgrade and the like.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:03:05-07:00","id":1480406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480398#post1480398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably don't want to engage a hard determinist on the topic of free will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I don't think you or I have anything like the libertarian free will that most people mean when they talk about free will, so the question is pretty meaningless to me. Also, as was pointed out above, <i>Freak Legion</i> (which I seem to remember you were fond of) certainly assumes that fomori are playable.<br /> <br /> I'm just curious why you continue to insist that Souleaters are silly but Banes are (presumably?) fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The difference between V:TM and W:TA</b><br /> <br /> Well focusing on that, I suppose it's not just what VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE is but also what WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE is. I've mentioned that V:TM is Gothic Punk horror fiction about sin, damnation, and remorse from your activities. It is about coping with a dreadful curse and dealing with the fact that you are now divorced from whoever you are while alive. Also, the fact that you are immortal and trapped in a feudalist exploitative super-capitalist society where the rich are literal predators on the poor.<br /> <br /> W:TA by contrast is Tragic Heroic Mythology. Whereas vampire is Jane Eye, Wuthering Heights, and The Anarchist's Cookbook, W:TA is Beowulf, Oedipus Rex, and Last of the Mohicans. Werewolves have a lot of curse-like elements but their actual curse is the fact that they are going to lose Ragnarok and die fighting the Dragon and realize they've married their mother.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't have the kind of self-loathing narcissistic tragedy that vampires do and, generally, all love being werewolves (I'm simplifying). They, however, are destined to throw themselves into the jaws of death to try to save the world. In V:TM, you are the monster. In Werewolf, you are not THE monster but slay the monster. It's just THE monster is going to win.<br /> <br /> Souleaters don't work for V:TM because, while there's nothing wrong with it, <i>Angel: The Series</i> is not how you're meant to run being undead. Generally, most vampires are not heroes and fighting evil. A single vampire or coterie of vampires fighting evil is fine, I've run many a game like that but they're an aberration. Most vampires do not give a shit and if they found out there was a corporation making a deal with Satan to make more money, 50% of all vampires would react with, &quot;Okay, THAT is a hot stock tip. Where do I invest in this Pentex?&quot; Another 25% will go, &quot;Okay, not my problem.&quot; Another 10% will be like, &quot;Ah ha! A rival!&quot; With maybe 5% appropriately horrified.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Apocalypse, by contrast, is a game where you need an assortment of monsters and horrifying cannon fodder because they are defined by throwing themselves into the jaws of Fenris. It doesn't matter that Formori are victims of the Wyrm, they're people to be killed because a werewolf lives for violence and dies by violence.<br /> <br /> At least that's my view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480402#post1480402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It sort of depends. The Possessed book for Year of the Damned had rules for Autonomy, how much free will a host still had from their Bane (or its Weaver or Wyld counterpart), including the suggestion of doing something similar to Wraith's Shadowguiding when running Possessed characters in a game. Generally, the more powerful a Fomori is, the less Autonomy it likely has, but that may not always be true. You can also give up Autonomy to get rid of deformities, so you could have a low to mid powered Fomori who looks totally human but is all but lost to the Wyrm or a hideous monstrosity that is still human inside and would desperately like to be cured. This plays in to one of the Children of Gaia tribe's schticks about believing they should try to save and cure/heal (physically, mentally, and spiritually) Fomori whenever possible instead of simply killing them. While you undoubtedly have a lot of Fomori who are eager volunteers for Pentex supersoldier programs, members of corrupt cults, and general reprobates, you also have no small amount of poor schlubs who are victims of bad luck, accidents, or just an uncaring world. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is entirely feasible for a werewolf pack to come across The Toxic Avenger, an accidentally created Fomori set on being a vigilante against Pentex and street crime, who could be a potential ally but who is almost certain to come to a tragic end. Likewise, it is entirely possible to have an all Fomori game that draws on things like Fight Club, Venom, Upgrade and the like.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I should clarify I like Freak Legion just fine.<br /> <br /> However, when I highlight &quot;free will&quot; let's just say I'm saying capacity for self-reflection and change. When I do my occassional Formori character, I highlight them as either an exception or someone on the fast slide to the same fate that awaits most vampires: death or damnation. Venom is a good example of a Formori but he's someone who will either be eventually destroyed by his bond with his symbiote (spiritually or otherwise) or is a wholly rare example of a human being who can hold out against it while 99% of them do not.<br /> <br /> Either way, the issue is not that an alien thing is eating away at your soul--that's what a vampire is as mentioned.<br /> <br /> It's that vampires slaying Formori is basically making vampires the lesser evil and giving them a pass on their own evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2022, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:11:54-07:00","id":1480408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480397#post1480397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, experimenting with the Tzimisce would probably remove some of my issues if they would stop trying to make them WEIRD AND CREEPY as if that was the only way to do them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess that the first thing to spring to mind when reading that sentence was the idea of Adult Wednesday Addams (more the tv version) as a Tzimisce. Probably just focused on Animalism and Auspex, and being this mix of extremely curious and frequently deadpan about everything. Oddly anachronistic, but deeply devoted to her ghoul spider Homer. And if in the Camarilla, a Keeper of Elysium. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:16:39-07:00","id":1480410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480408#post1480408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I confess that the first thing to spring to mind when reading that sentence was the idea of Adult Wednesday Addams (more the tv version) as a Tzimisce. Probably just focused on Animalism and Auspex, and being this mix of extremely curious and frequently deadpan about everything. Oddly anachronistic, but deeply devoted to her ghoul spider Homer. And if in the Camarilla, a Keeper of Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>back in the 90s there was a fun adaptation of the Addams Family as a Sabbat pack living in an old mansion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:24:43-07:00","id":1480412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480410#post1480410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> back in the 90s there was a fun adaptation of the Addams Family as a Sabbat pack living in an old mansion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember that. I just can't remember where it was from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T15:29:07-07:00","id":1480415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480406#post1480406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least that's my view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, you have a perfectly valid take on the different game lines -- but in order to have that take, is it necessary to keep calling Souleaters a silly idea? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As far as I can see, they are no more campy or stupid than Banes are, and Vicissitude users are no more ridiculous or overplayed than fomori are.<br /> <br /> The reason we don't see eye to eye on the matter is that I <i>don't</i> make a radical distinction between the different World of Darkness game lines. The early writers (circa 1991-1994) were certainly not averse to true crossovers -- the early 90s products are full of suggestions for crossover chronicles, and there are entire sourcebooks such as <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i> and <i>Necropolis: Atlanta</i> devoted to crossover play.<br /> <br /> It was only during the Revised era that White Wolf took a different view on the matter, and the people in charge started to push the idea that combining the different game lines diluted the themes and concepts of each game. Well, I simply disagree -- my chronicles have always assumed that Kindred, Garou, Mages, Wraiths, and so on exist in the same setting, not in some kind of different but overlapping realities. I haven't noticed my games suffering as a result.<br /> <br /> In my World of Darkness, there absolutely is <i>something</i> otherworldly and hideously corrupt seeping through the cracks of reality in the deep background of the setting. Some of the supernatural factions are more aware of this phenomenon than others, but it doesn't change the fact that this presence is assumed to be there at all times.<br /> <br /> Given this is the case, why <i>wouldn't</i> I include the element in my Vampire games? Call it the Wyrm, call it Souleaters, call it Nephandi, or whatever -- as far as I can see, shared concepts like this do not dilute the primary themes of each game to any noticeable degree. Obviously your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, it's a little exhausting to be told year after year that actually what I'm doing is silly and wrongheaded and it would be better if all such material was retconned out of existence. It also doesn't seem to matter how many times I try to articulate that it is perfectly possible to use ideas such as Souleaters in a thoughtful and narratively satisfying manner -- sooner or later the discussion always defaults back to &quot;Souleaters silly, <i>DSotBH</i> bad.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T15:36:45-07:00","id":1480416,"title":"","content":"What Free Will even means when talking about roleplay? Setting aside the fact that no character has Free Will, as they follow the Will of the players, and me being also a Determinist who find the very notion of Free Will quite misleading, what's really the difference between roleplaying a free person, roleplaying a person loosing freedom to an alien mind, and roleplaying the alien mind itself? They are all characters perfectly fit for roleplay. Hell, DtF specifically puts you to play as a possessed person roleplaying the possessor spirit.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, &quot;alien&quot; is a complicated concept here. I agree that in the end WoD mostly uses &quot;alien&quot; to mean &quot;without empathy&quot;, but I find it outright stupid. A lot of real people has problems with empathy of one sort or another, some are completely devoid of empathy, and they don't behave as Tzimisce. Contrary to popular belief they're not even particularly prone to violent crime. &quot;Alien&quot; is used in a lot of contexts that together just means &quot;I, the author, don't think this is normal, but don't want to call it madness either&quot;. That's silly.<br /> <br /> Few characters have much of a reason to be actually said to have an alien mindset, and usually the Tzimisce aren't among those. Their affectation and love for body horror for the sake of it are pretty human traits, or at least something only a human-made mind would have. I wouldn't call the Wamphyri a well done example of an &quot;alien&quot; mindset and I don't think they're a serious exploration (which doesn't mean they're not a good exploration, parody and satire are perfectly fine), and while the Tzimisce are a strong nod to Necroscope, they're not actual Wamphyri levels of inhuman unless you take choice bits of presentation and lore and run them to the extreme, while ignoring other pieces, like the many, many characters and clan descriptions, especially from DA, that have a more Old Clan vibe to them while still having Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> But that's that. I don't particularly like the Necroscope-style Tzimisce and I don't like the Souleaters. Like, in <b><u>I</u></b> don't like. No problem whatsoever with other people liking and doing them, even in my games. It fits the setting as much as anything else, it is an RPG setting and isn't nor should be limited just to its main genre. I don't call their style &quot;alien&quot; or &quot;weird&quot;, but whatever. I think assuming vampires of all clans as Humans First creates a more interesting exploration, narrative and is more realistic psychologically speaking, but that's only relevant for my own games.<br /> <br /> There are only two point in all this that really merit more attention. My greatest distaste with Souleaters isn't they bringing the option to make &quot;weird&quot; Tzimisce, it is their forcing this through Vicissitude. I think that runs the risk of greatly reducing the range of character options. And the problem with the idea of &quot;alien&quot; runs deep, but it is something I would need more space and effort to explain than I'm willing to spend now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T15:42:07-07:00","id":1480418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480416#post1480416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Free Will even means when talking about roleplay? Setting aside the fact that no character has Free Will, as they follow the Will of the players, and me being also a Determinist who find the very notion of Free Will quite misleading, what's really the difference between roleplaying a free person, roleplaying a person loosing freedom to an alien mind, and roleplaying the alien mind itself? They are all characters perfectly fit for roleplay. Hell, DtF specifically puts you to play as a possessed person roleplaying the possessor spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion on Determinalism is oddly best summarized by the fact that I come from a family of alcoholics and substance abusers. Whether or not the people in my family can choose or not to become addicted is ultimately irrelevant on a basic level but they have had members who did NOT choose to get help and get better and have had members who HAVE made the long and difficult choice to get better with meetings/effort/programs.<br /> <br /> Choice is EXTREMELY important in arguing with them about whether to take that next drink, or, indeed, the first one. It has defined much of my family history and childhood to adult life.<br /> <br /> So while philosophically it may make a difference whether you have no free will or not, I absolutely have lived 40 years among people who very much have the APPEARANCE to themselves of making choices over whether to fight their addictions or not.<br /> <br /> And since I associate V:TM with addiction as a theme (backed up by the game), it is very much an important theme.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;If choice is an illusion, it doesn't matter because it's a good illusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480415#post1480415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, you have a perfectly valid take on the different game lines -- but in order to have that take, is it necessary to keep calling Souleaters a silly idea? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As far as I can see, they are no more campy or stupid than Banes are, and Vicissitude users are no more ridiculous or overplayed than fomori are</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, I take back my statement souleaters are silly.<br /> <br /> For me, I felt it was one concept too many for DIRTY SECRETS OF THE BLACK HAND. They were already a vampire illuminati (who were, themselves, humanity's Illuminati) and playing both the Sabbat vs. the Camarilla while serving the Antediluvians. The Souleaters felt like they were adding an additional conflict to the story that wasn't thematic with them being an insane Gehenna cult and seemed to exist primarily to make them seem more like &quot;good guys&quot; when they were a bunch of nutters who kidnapped children, indoctrinated them in HELL, and raised them to be vampires.<br /> <br /> But it's okay because they fight the aliens possessing people.<br /> <br /> I may not have given them a fair shake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2022, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T16:45:48-07:00","id":1480425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480418#post1480418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since I associate V:TM with addiction as a theme (backed up by the game), it is very much an important theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Determinist does not mean I can't see the value of choice, both as a theme and as many other things, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> The point is that seeing choice as a relevant theme for the setting is a very different thing from saying a lack of choice makes a character impossible to roleplay. The two statements are a world apart. Even because those characters can still work with the theme of choice. Do you chose to fight the alien urge or do you chose to give in? Do you chose to revel in it? Do you chose to try to save as much as you can from your humanity? Do you chose to investigate further your actual nature? Even if you're the possessor entity, do you chose to follow your previous dictates or to let your host change you? There are still many choices to be taken by a character that seems defined by a lack of choice, which isn't different from a vampire that can't chose to not be an undead cannibal with an inner Beast, but can chose a lot about where to take this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T16:48:42-07:00","id":1480426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480425#post1480425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Determinist does not mean I can't see the value of choice, both as a theme and as many other things, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> The point is that seeing choice as a relevant theme for the setting is a very different thing from saying a lack of choice makes a character impossible to roleplay. The two statements are a world apart. Even because those characters can still work with the theme of choice. Do you chose to fight the alien urge or do you chose to give in? Do you chose to revel in it? Do you chose to try to save as much as you can from your humanity? Do you chose to investigate further your actual nature? Even if you're the possessor entity, do you chose to follow your previous dictates or to let your host change you? There are still many choices to be taken by a character that seems defined by a lack of choice, which isn't different from a vampire that can't chose to not be an undead cannibal with an inner Beast, but can chose a lot about where to take this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.<br /> <br /> I suppose I simply don't think the way I see Formori is something that have a personality interesting to play. A true Formori in my games is not a person without empathy. It does not care about others, true. But it does not care about ANYTHING. Even itself. It does not care about family, it has no favorite foods, it doesn't appreciate art, it does not feel guilt, friendship. It exists, sort of like a philosophical zombie, as a hollow shell expressing its particular form of evil.<br /> <br /> Why did you kill that baby?<br /> <br /> Because it was there.<br /> <br /> They are philosophical zombies empty of what once made them people and have no inner life, just purpose to spread their Bane's type of horror.<br /> <br /> The people BECOMING Formori are people that are interesting to play and perhaps resisting but they are doomed in their onw way unless the Bane is killed by the Garou or somehow exorcised.<br /> <br /> This is also PURELY HOW I DO IT and not meant to restrain anyone else's idea of canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2022, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T18:47:07-07:00","id":1480437,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's not how I do it. Mind you, I go 5 plus year stretches without running fomori games, but when I do, I run them as possessing free will. Because Freak Legion makes it seem like they have free will. And I just took that as canon a long time ago and that's been that. So the, literally maybe 5 times in the entire history of the WOD that I've run fomori games, I've run them as having free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T18:50:30-07:00","id":1480438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480437#post1480437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, that's not how I do it. Mind you, I go 5 plus year stretches without running fomori games, but when I do, I run them as possessing free will. Because Freak Legion makes it seem like they have free will. And I just took that as canon a long time ago and that's been that. So the, literally maybe 5 times in the entire history of the WOD that I've run fomori games, I've run them as having free will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think canonically some do and others are mindless puppets of their banes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T19:15:04-07:00","id":1480439,"title":"","content":"I do find that fomori make for kind of interesting everyman stories. They are the ultimate losers, the Charlie Browns of the WOD. I actually kinda feel like running a fomori game now. But I'm already running two vampire games, so I don't know when I would fit a fomori game in. Still, if I do run a fomori game again one of these days, I'm going to play up the Charlie Brown nature of their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T19:43:27-07:00","id":1480442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480439#post1480439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find that fomori make for kind of interesting everyman stories. They are the ultimate losers, the Charlie Browns of the WOD. I actually kinda feel like running a fomori game now. But I'm already running two vampire games, so I don't know when I would fit a fomori game in. Still, if I do run a fomori game again one of these days, I'm going to play up the Charlie Brown nature of their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big thing I do when I do insert Formori characters with free will is I emphasize the ticking clock nature of their story. Unlike vampires who have immortality and vast powers as well as a heroin/sex-like kiss, being a Formori sucks. Even if you somehow are able to pass for a human being, you're slowly being eaten out from the inside by a monster and eventually will either be replaced or turn into something unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> A bit like Call of Cthulhu, it's not IF you'll lose your character, it's when.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T20:28:13-07:00","id":1480443,"title":"","content":"I don't do it that way. The physical grossness of their existence is sufficient horror without introducing vampire-like beast-angst. In my very few fomori games, being a fomori is purely about body horror. Vomiting acid randomly or having a face on your stomach that constantly makes cruel jokes at your expense is plenty horrific without them needing any extra element of horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T13:07:56-07:00","id":1480473,"title":"","content":"&gt;&gt;&gt;deleted, it's covered&lt;&lt;&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-08-2022, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T13:57:06-07:00","id":1480476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480443#post1480443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't do it that way. The physical grossness of their existence is sufficient horror without introducing vampire-like beast-angst. In my very few fomori games, being a fomori is purely about body horror. Vomiting acid randomly or having a face on your stomach that constantly makes cruel jokes at your expense is plenty horrific without them needing any extra element of horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. For me, losing control of your mind is greater horror. That you can no longer control your actions.<br /> <br /> But each has interesting opportunities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T14:27:19-07:00","id":1480480,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the shout out, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/382103/Hunger-from-Beyond-for-V5\" target=\"_blank\">The book he references can be found here</a>.)<br /> <br /> My own issue with the Tzimisce in the past is that for all that could be done with them, they were rather one note. Just a bunch of sado-masochism fetishists with tentacles. That is only striking once and quickly becomes neither frightening nor memorable. It also stops being &quot;alien&quot; almost immediately. The entire set up can also become cheap and comic quickly.<br /> <br /> The fiends should have been presented with a subtler touch. Let the strangeness, and alien qualities in body and mind, slowly be revealed.<br /> <br /> There is something potentially tragic in that the Tzimisce are desperate to give up humanity in body, mind and soul - but for all of that they cannot escape from humanity (and morality) and still retain their identity. To truly escape means they can simply consumed by the monstrosity of their line. Which the Sabbat is rebelling against.<br /> <br /> But generally the nuance and possibility were rejected for an SnM freakshow at the top of its lungs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T14:53:53-07:00","id":1480483,"title":"","content":"I think vampires can be alienness but they're more like the Deep Ones or ghouls in that they're close enough to be inhuman to humans but still HUMAN.<br /> <br /> Unlike the spirits and demons that are wholly unlike mankind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T15:48:39-07:00","id":1480486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480476#post1480476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. For me, losing control of your mind is greater horror. That you can no longer control your actions.<br /> <br /> But each has interesting opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may well be the &quot;greater horror&quot;. I don't care. I'm not competing in a greatest horror contest. I'm trying to have fun playing the Charlie Brown of the WOD. Something like having a second head that constantly makes jokes at your expense is plenty horrific enough for that purpose. If I wanted to win a greatest horror contest, I'd do something like a game about people in Hell suffering in an agony that begins at aleph null and then moves on to the powerset of aleph null agony, then the powerset of that, then the powerset of that, increasing the agony by another order of magnitude past infinity every attosecond forever. But that's not my goal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T16:26:40-07:00","id":1480488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480486#post1480486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may well be the &quot;greater horror&quot;. I don't care. I'm not competing in a greatest horror contest. I'm trying to have fun playing the Charlie Brown of the WOD. Something like having a second head that constantly makes jokes at your expense is plenty horrific enough for that purpose. If I wanted to win a greatest horror contest, I'd do something like a game about people in Hell suffering in an agony that begins at aleph null and then moves on to the powerset of aleph null agony, then the powerset of that, then the powerset of that, increasing the agony by another order of magnitude past infinity every attosecond forever. But that's not my goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I didn't mean to give the impression I was arguing let alone competing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T20:22:28-07:00","id":1480508,"title":"","content":"In concept, the Tzimisce are interesting. They're one of my favorites in Dark Ages, and in modern nights they have had a massive fall from &quot;grace&quot;. The problem isn't the Tzimisce themselves, but the players. I've seen a lot of PC Tzimisce, and they all tend to be pretty one-note: a weirdo doctor if they're &quot;good&quot; or a weirdo nightmare if they're not. It all gets very samey and, yes, boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T23:25:11-07:00","id":1480514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480396#post1480396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, if I was a writer on Werewolf, I'd make the Werewolves more prone to being criticized (it's already halfway to the Sabbat) and monsters more ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's definitely a lot to criticize, and early Werewolf material is fairly blatant about. 1e is all about Garou society being too out of date and too hidebound. Just like 1e Vampire really encouraged PCs to be Anarchs, 1e Werewolf encouraged PCs to be critical of Garou society. But that wasn't followed through.<br /> <br /> I think one of the reasons is that the black and white nature of Garou society was something many players liked. They liked a simple Law versus Chaos narrative.<br /> <br /> Another reason is that many STs and PCs did not want self-critical games. I see all sorts of asshole PCs in Vampire. I rarely see them in Werewolf. If you have a LARP or Online Game in Vampire, you'll find many PC concepts that are villainous. You'll see many analogues to canon NPCs that are antagonists. Asshold Ventrue Prince wannabees. Shitheel Setites. Narcissistic Toreadors that put the Heathers to shame. Power hungry, untrustworthy Tremere. And so on. If go to LARP or Online Games of Werewolf, you won't. You won't find the Shadow Lord PCs conspiring with vampires of other Wyrm minions. You won't find insane Silver Fang kings screaming about lese majeste. You won't find narrow minded Fianna bigots discriminating against Metis. And so on. Instead, everyone is a fairly reasonable and open minded 21st century Western moderate instead of an old style pre-modern people of an aristocratic warrior culture.<br /> <br /> But that is more about players than the setting itself. Though I agree Revised deliberately downplayed the more objectionable elements of Garou society and the setting. It's one reason I really liked 1e's depiction of the less savory rampant crime and collaboration of its members with their race's enemies and against their own laws, and every tribe nursing ancient grudges against one or more other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T05:57:41-07:00","id":1480528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480514#post1480514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's definitely a lot to criticize, and early Werewolf material is fairly blatant about. 1e is all about Garou society being too out of date and too hidebound. Just like 1e Vampire really encouraged PCs to be Anarchs, 1e Werewolf encouraged PCs to be critical of Garou society. But that wasn't followed through.<br /> <br /> I think one of the reasons is that the black and white nature of Garou society was something many players liked. They liked a simple Law versus Chaos narrative.<br /> <br /> Another reason is that many STs and PCs did not want self-critical games. I see all sorts of asshole PCs in Vampire. I rarely see them in Werewolf. If you have a LARP or Online Game in Vampire, you'll find many PC concepts that are villainous. You'll see many analogues to canon NPCs that are antagonists. Asshold Ventrue Prince wannabees. Shitheel Setites. Narcissistic Toreadors that put the Heathers to shame. Power hungry, untrustworthy Tremere. And so on. If go to LARP or Online Games of Werewolf, you won't. You won't find the Shadow Lord PCs conspiring with vampires of other Wyrm minions. You won't find insane Silver Fang kings screaming about lese majeste. You won't find narrow minded Fianna bigots discriminating against Metis. And so on. Instead, everyone is a fairly reasonable and open minded 21st century Western moderate instead of an old style pre-modern people of an aristocratic warrior culture.<br /> <br /> But that is more about players than the setting itself. Though I agree Revised deliberately downplayed the more objectionable elements of Garou society and the setting. It's one reason I really liked 1e's depiction of the less savory rampant crime and collaboration of its members with their race's enemies and against their own laws, and every tribe nursing ancient grudges against one or more other tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well vampire doesn't really reward being saintly. Golconda is so hard that it's not really a viable goal. Humanity loss isn't a big deal until it gets extremely low, something even ruthless political schemers rarely suffer.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile werewolves get actual superpowers if they sincerely play their characters as true believing superheroes. The entire renown system is geared towards encouraging Super-Friends behavior, so a you get a lot of Super-Friends werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T07:17:05-07:00","id":1480533,"title":"","content":"OK, Tzimisce and the alien nature of vampires. I actually feel like hyperfocusing on vicissitude as a blatantly obvious &quot;freak show&quot; body-horror discipline makes the Tzimisce <i>less</i> creepy/alien (it is fun sometimes, though). I have it that such uses are considered immature, and a sign that one is a fledgling who by so fervently rejecting a human shape is still defining themselves by humanity. Older Tzimisce have come to understand that their human shell is simply a tool. It isn't what they are, any more than the light at the front of an anglerfish is the fish. Or, for a closer example, a large blue butterfly larva appears to ants like an ant larva, which it uses to inflitrate ant nests and prey on the ants who have been fooled into thinking it's one of them. A caterpillar isn't a baby ant, a vampire isn't a human.<br /> <br /> The horror of vampires, for kine and even many kindred, is the uncanny valley effect and the fear of parasites. It looks human, it can think like a human, yes. Because it's an act by a specialised predator that utilises aggressive mimicry to hunt humans. The body it inhabits is <i>dead</i>. The vampire is the thing<i> inside </i>the corpse. Their reproductive process is parasitical and we're the host species. Lucky us!<br /> Their faux-humanity is exactly what makes vampires alien horrors, in my view, and vicissitude is the exaggeration of that. Not an obvious threat at first glance, there's no reason to have your guard up. The edits are a subtle advantage and rarely come out until it's too late when the deception is revealed and <i>oh god no</i>. Edit your joints to move in for inhuman range and flexibility. Alter your vocal chords to sound like someone or something else. Maybe adjust your voice to a permanent pitch that triggers ASMR to endear, relax and further manipulate your prey, or distort it to induce a fear response. Limbs, necks and waists that rotate 360\u00b0 or whatever the hell you want to do that gives you an advantage.<br /> But their biggest advantage is that unlike most vampires, who steal one person's identity at their birth, Tzimisce can do this as much as they damn well want.<br /> <br /> A Tzimisce can kill you, trade faces with you, and steal your whole life <i>without anybody ever knowing</i>. Works on kindred too. Announce at Elysium that the court has been infiltrated by Tzimisce. We don't know how many or whose face they're using. Any and all signs of people acting &quot;out of character&quot; are now worthy of pitchforks and torches. Enjoy your paranoia. In some ways they're better at camoflauge than obfuscate and protean users. They make wonderful spies and assassins.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasitic pseudohuman mimics that modify and utilitse their host bodies as tools, and the Tzimisce are the epitome of this. They can explore and evolve the nature of vampirism to a greater extent than their cousins.<br /> Nah, I think vicissitude is great. As far as I'm concerned, Old Clan Tzimisce is nothing special and is as limiting a concept as the vicissitude monsters. But that said, I can kind of see both being redundant. If I were to cut down on the clans, I think Old Clan would be a Ventrue bloodline and vicissitude users would be merged with the Gangrel or reclassified as one of their bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Edit: but the territoriality is also an important aspect of the clan, and V5's take on their weakness is the one I use. I just don't like that aspect of them being limited to &quot;one-note Dracula rip off&quot; any more than I like vicissitude being reduced to splatterpunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-09-2022, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T08:20:10-07:00","id":1480542,"title":"","content":"Thinking back, I don't think my first encounters with Tzimisce was a positive one, much like the Sabbat as given for the first and second editions of VtM. I think someone said splatterpunk before, and I think that is a good description. Not my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> However, with the release of the Vampire: the Dark Ages, something much better came out, and for a while it was a much better clan. It felt like they did something great with what they had to work with from the legacy of The Players Handbook to the Sabbat. We got characters such as Rustovich, Radu and Vykos, who at least at this stage were not simply defined by a single discipline. There was some variations, naturally, memory is best when looked at with a less critical eye. They were a noble but still ruthless clan. Tradition meant something.<br /> With revenants added (in Ghouls: Fatal Addiction, if I remember correctly?), this put a whole new layer to the Tzimisce and the way they lorded over their ghouls and lands. Not everything was based on Vicissitude. There were still the monstrosities, if you wanted that aspect, but there were choices.<br /> I'll bring up the Dirty Secrets. There seems to be two camps, those who enjoyed it, and those who did not. I am part of the camp that did not enjoy it. The best part of the book was the Old Clan Tzimisce. Perhaps this was what the Dark Ages used as a foundation for the clan?<br /> <br /> Then came the revised editions. To its credit, it mostly made the Sabbat playable, and by that Tzimisce. On the other hand, it started to snowball, with more and more focus about Vicissitude. They have an entire Path that requires the Discipline. I do not necessarily feel this is something strange, as with every discipline, there is bound to be a morality if it is pushed to far, and I would love to have seen the same work with other disciplines - particularly the common ones. But Tzimisce, at this point, had just one clan discipline, and two other that were cheaper. It was never a discussion if a Tzimisce was going to have Vicissitude, but rather how they were going to work in having Body Crafts into their concept. I felt the foundation Vampire: the Dark Ages was being eroded, and I lost interest in the Clan.<br /> <br /> In the end, we had a hiatus due to the world ending and all that, but old habits die hard. Ran a Sabbat campaign where only &quot;the common eight&quot; disciplines were available, and had someone directly drawn to Tzimisce with no Vicissitude. It was nice to run tyrannical Tzimisce and not having to figure out how they would out-do each other in freakshow.<br /> <br /> I read the V20 versions. It is nice to see love for a game that I played so much in my youth, but life had gotten in the way at this point for gaming.<br /> <br /> On to V5. They captured what I like most about Tzimisce. Vicissitude is still there, but it is an expensive option. Expensive as in the powers given up. I do not think trading Dominate for Auspex undervalues them at all. The Tzimisce were, in my opinion, made awesome despite their disciplines, not because. They resemble much more a feral VtR Ventrue now, which once again, in my opinion is a clear upgrade that this is the 'default' Tzimisce, not the 'splatterpunk' Tzimisce - but again, this is my opinion.<br /> That V5 requires a human touchstone would somehow remove the playability of Tzimisce as they are to 'cold and callous' is something I would consider a fallacy. While this may be a correct stereotype for the Sabbat/&quot;old world&quot; Tzimisce, it is not true on an individual level. The way touchstones are setup is to play young vampires in a Camarilla or Anarch setting. It is a highly flexible and independent system, where it is quite possible to both remove and replace parts of it at to better suit the theme and mood that one wishes to play by. I think in general this is a major strength with V5, as it is very modular, something apparently the credit goes to Kenneth Hite for.<br /> <br /> They have been a favorite clan of mine, and I would say despite their disciplines. Successively, it became less of a clan and more of a discipline, and for me, that lost my interest. The same goes for a lot of Clans. The number of Tremere characters without Thaumaturgy could probably be counted on one hand, and an arguments could be made for every bloodline, Ravnos, Giovanni, Dementation Malkavians. Lasombra were successively pushed into this niche as well, partly because of the strong mechanics of Obtenebration, but also because of paths and abyss rituals and what not.<br /> Once a discipline becomes this integrated and critical into a clan, it is my opinion that it looses something and the whole becomes a lot less.<br /> In V5, I think the Tzimisce once again back on the right track. Or at least the track I find interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T11:22:53-07:00","id":1480676,"title":"","content":"I think there is some errors and excesses on the Clan truly, and sometimes they are too much of a villainous enemy of the good people and all that is good in this God's green earth. And hell, the way it is portrayed I think they are worst than the Baali sometimes, only more violent and profane than the Setites, but even more warmongering than the Haquimites. And they don't like many of the more 'popular' and gregarious Clans. So yeah, they kind of feel like something that needs more practicality or else would've ended up being the enemy of everyone (besides itself). <br /> <br /> So, they are either the strongest Clan ever because they fight everyone and everything even more than the Brujah, or they are a bunch of stupid cringe-like sadists that are demon-fodder of Kupala and alike. Sabbat's new Tzimisces really have fallen from the great voivodes of old, becoming shock and stock troops.<br /> <br /> But, they unite a lot of what makes vampires and Vampire as a whole and interesting theme and game/setting. So if we would scrape the setting to a minimium number of Clans, I would definetely keep them, cuz they have a ton of venues to tread. I won't even begging to list the amount of evocation and mystery, while also giving the lordly and macabre but noble feel of vampires, the Tzimisce can attain.<br /> <br /> They got too much spotlight, but ended up being the common go-to enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T12:01:00-07:00","id":1480684,"title":"","content":"I think the clan is alright as it captures a bit of what a &quot;Dracula's clan&quot; would be. But then Vicissitude went in a more disturbing alien feel, etc. But I have no problems with the clan as a whole. One thing I REALLY HATE about them is the idea that came, I think, with revised, that the Tzimisce antediluvian was &quot;everywhere&quot;, like a seed in anyone who ever experienced blood &quot;tainted&quot;, etc. I really hate the idea of making the Tzimisce antediluvian a &quot;world eating&quot; abomination that is beyond any other antediluvian or basically anything in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T16:49:49-07:00","id":1480703,"title":"","content":"I think assigning Dracula's clan as Tzimisce did a disservice to Dracula, Tzimisce and the game in general. Quite a few clans embodied at least as many Dracula aspects as does Tzimisce; Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Tremere, Ventrue...hell, even Brujah and Ravnos have distinct Dracula aspects. They should have left his clan an item of contention, with multiple clans claiming and/or blaming, as the case fit. Trying to make the Tzimisce clan fit the man or vice versa leaves something less than the sum of its parts.<br /> <br /> But it's worth noting that in the books, Dracula is not a typical Tzimisce, and is disliked/scoffed at by most of the clan. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T17:27:11-07:00","id":1480705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480703#post1480703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think assigning Dracula's clan as Tzimisce did a disservice to Dracula, Tzimisce and the game in general. Quite a few clans embodied at least as many Dracula aspects as does Tzimisce; Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Tremere, Ventrue...hell, even Brujah and Ravnos have distinct Dracula aspects. They should have left his clan an item of contention, with multiple clans claiming and/or blaming, as the case fit. Trying to make the Tzimisce clan fit the man or vice versa leaves something less than the sum of its parts.<br /> <br /> But it's worth noting that in the books, Dracula is not a typical Tzimisce, and is disliked/scoffed at by most of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't particularly see a problem with Tzimisce being a Dracula, but I can see your point. The thing that annoys me most is some ramifications of Vicissitude that were way too &quot;bizarre&quot; to my taste and the fact that their Antediluvian is such a bizarre apocalyptic Cthulhu beast...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T18:08:11-07:00","id":1480708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480514#post1480514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's definitely a lot to criticize, and early Werewolf material is fairly blatant about. 1e is all about Garou society being too out of date and too hidebound. Just like 1e Vampire really encouraged PCs to be Anarchs, 1e Werewolf encouraged PCs to be critical of Garou society. But that wasn't followed through.<br /> <br /> I think one of the reasons is that the black and white nature of Garou society was something many players liked. They liked a simple Law versus Chaos narrative</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big difference, ultimately, is the overall storyline. In Werewolf you're playing monsters, but monsters who ultimately make the world a better place. If the Garou all vanished, companies like Pentex would be free to run roughshod over everything, and that would be horrific. As bad as werewolves can be, ultimately the world is a better place because they exist.<br /> <br /> Conversely, vampires are parasites who drink blood and manipulate humans. They're monsters and the world is worse because of it. You may have the rare example of a vampire who spends his unlife trying to improve the lives of those around him, or vampires who use their powers to destroy evil beings, but they're very much exceptions. And Kindred don't even have the plausibility of Wan Kuei, where a Devil Tiger can justify their actions by pointing towards their battle against the Yama Kings, or the need for devils to inflict punishment on humanity, as proof that they're making the world a better place.<br /> <br /> Ultimately even when the Garou elders are hidebound, they're still fighting the good fight and whatnot. And werewolf players are encouraged to make characters that will be putting the good of Gaia and the good of other werewolves first, rather than playing the character who is out for numero uno. Vampires are definitely not fighting the good fight, and when making a vampire, there's no narrative pressure to make one who's putting the good of humanity first or anything like that. So vampire players are more free to play selfish assholes than Garou since even a selfish asshole Garou is, narratively, still balanced by the fact that he's putting his life on the line to fight greater evils to save the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-10-2022, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T20:32:58-07:00","id":1480720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480705#post1480705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly see a problem with Tzimisce being a Dracula, but I can see your point. The thing that annoys me most is some ramifications of Vicissitude that were way too &quot;bizarre&quot; to my taste and the fact that their Antediluvian is such a bizarre apocalyptic Cthulhu beast...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think [Tzimisce] as a Lovecraftian Great One was a bad thing by itself. I surely agree that sometimes it was heavy-handed and there should be more mystery around it, but giving a sample form to the horror the Ante is supposed to be made it far more palpable, and makes a lot of sense as vampiric legend.<br /> <br /> It is actually the lack of such a form of horrific apotheosis that seems frustrating for most Antes. We're told that they're out to eat their progeny and end the world, but just by being... older? While their In-Clan Discipline spreads gave us something to imagine, there's actually very little to picture how the world ending under [Ventrue], Arikel or Ennoya looks like. That was only barely addressed in Gehenna itself, but that's not just about what form they'll effectively take in the end, it is about what imagery stories about the end conjure for them, this we have nothing on those and many other Antes.<br /> <br /> Sutekh is a powerful sorcerer and cult leader about whom we have many and varied stories that help picture what his raise could look like, if just to explore the legends in a game. [Tzimisce] has a powerful image as this eldritch abomination, somewhat compensating for the lack of variety. What the others have? Even the Malkavian Network is too abstract and vague a threat, and [Ravnos] just a heavy metal week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:22:42-07:00","id":1480723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480720#post1480720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't think [Tzimisce] as a Lovecraftian Great One was a bad thing by itself. I surely agree that sometimes it was heavy-handed and there should be more mystery around it, but giving a sample form to the horror the Ante is supposed to be made it far more palpable, and makes a lot of sense as vampiric legend.<br /> <br /> It is actually the lack of such a form of horrific apotheosis that seems frustrating for most Antes. We're told that they're out to eat their progeny and end the world, but just by being... older? While their In-Clan Discipline spreads gave us something to imagine, there's actually very little to picture how the world ending under [Ventrue], Arikel or Ennoya looks like. That was only barely addressed in Gehenna itself, but that's not just about what form they'll effectively take in the end, it is about what imagery stories about the end conjure for them, this we have nothing on those and many other Antes.<br /> <br /> Sutekh is a powerful sorcerer and cult leader about whom we have many and varied stories that help picture what his raise could look like, if just to explore the legends in a game. [Tzimisce] has a powerful image as this eldritch abomination, somewhat compensating for the lack of variety. What the others have? Even the Malkavian Network is too abstract and vague a threat, and [Ravnos] just a heavy metal week.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand your point, and you raised an interesting observation. My main problem with the Tzimisce &quot;Lovecraftian Great One&quot; thing is that it makes it look like &quot;he/she/it&quot; is much more than the others, while it shouldn't be so IMO. But, as I said, you raised an interesting question that is the fact that we lack &quot;imagery&quot; for most of the &quot;Antes&quot; (although, to be fair, the fear of the &quot;Antes&quot; come much more from their sheer power and their will to destroy/subjugate the world than from their looks, as in some cases nobody would even know who or where the Ante is and that is fearsome as well).<br /> <br /> In terms of imagery, I like the Lasombra one even more than the Tzimisce one. I mean, a creature who merged with the Abyss and can be anything anywhere in the world and could just dominate the whole world like a dark lord or cast it into eternal darkness is also very interesting, but both are basically on the same level. Nosferatu is also one that strikes fear, btw for the opposite reason than Tzimisce. I think it's also very fearsome (possibly even more so) when we don't know and can't track where the enemy is. Some, I think, come off as &quot;too soft&quot; or &quot;too glamorous/sexy&quot;, but mostly because of the stereotypes associated with those clans, like Toreador or to some extent even Ventrue. Both clans very influenced by Anne Rice and the imagery associated with them (especially Toreador) doesn't usually strike fear as the others mentioned (I mean ,certainly Lestat is powerful and all, but he's so sexy I wouldn't mind much if he's a &quot;bad guy&quot; to me lol).<br /> <br /> All in all, you certainly came up with a good observation, perhaps it would have been better if we had more imagery of the Antediluvians, but as I said, we could see this through different angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:41:45-07:00","id":1480726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480720#post1480720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">picture how the world ending under [Ventrue], Arikel or Ennoya looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit side note, but always loved the Danava &quot;approach&quot; in this matter; the Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava. The Salubri say that Saulot achieved a transcendent spiritual state in the Indian city of Golconda, which falls within territory controlled by the Danava - some even believe that the very notion of Golconda originated from the Danava.<br /> Regal sages, ascetics and priests, the Danava are among the most respected vampires within the Caste system of the Indian Damned. Danava suffer from a variant weakness of the Ventrue Curse. Danava cannot gain sustenance from animal blood, with the blood of cows and pigs as the most grave taboo. If a Danava does not consecrate his victim to the gods in a ritual that lasts at very least 30 seconds, he only gains half as much blood points from it.<br /> This with their discipline spread of Dominate, Fortitude and Sadhana (Sadhana is a form of Hindu blood sorcery which predates the prominent Hermetic Thaumaturgy of the Tremere clan by thousands of years. It is practiced by the Hindu Brahmin Cainites of India, tho' the Blood Brahmins [sub sect] of India see themselves as demons, who seek to overthrow the gods and rule the universe in their stead by transcending the maya of the temporal world to achieve moksha)<br /> Suddenly would make things very... interesting<br /> Certanly more accepatble than a Ventrue Antediluvian that plays hide and seek and pretends to be dead, becasue tho' he was destroyed alegedly, had no problem to Embrace; last time 60 BC, hen he embraces Antonius and Erik Eigermann in Ancient Gaul.... not bad for a dead Antediluvian.<br /> Similarly how the Toreador actually have two antediluvian Arikel, the sculptor and Ishtar, the bull-dancer, usually they are belived the one and the same, just the geneology and time lines don't add up and diggin in the lore, it is clear, they are two seperate entities, and the Toreador are baranched from two ancient. Wich it self is funny and throws a curve ball to the whole &quot;what makes a clan a Clan debate&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-11-2022, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T21:58:31-07:00","id":1480728,"title":"","content":"Count me in as a fan of the Dark Ages Tzimisce, but not a fan of the modern Clan.<br /> <br /> That said, it is a bit of a shame that the Antes are seen as so much embodiment of the Clan with some Clans being considered better or worse than others instead of all Antes being beyond mortal comprehension of bad news.<br /> <br /> Speaking of [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] I personally dislike that they, unlike [Brujah], [Ventrue] and some more, could totally cheat death while an Ante was laid low in Carthage for real. The way I see it both [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] should be, and are, dead and gone regardless of what conspiracy and paranoid beliefs about them is propagated. It turned out that neither of them really was the kind of natural force they imagine themselves to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T06:24:11-07:00","id":1480741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480728#post1480728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Count me in as a fan of the Dark Ages Tzimisce, but not a fan of the modern Clan.<br /> <br /> That said, it is a bit of a shame that the Antes are seen as so much embodiment of the Clan with some Clans being considered better or worse than others instead of all Antes being beyond mortal comprehension of bad news.<br /> <br /> Speaking of [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] I personally dislike that they, unlike [Brujah], [Ventrue] and some more, could totally cheat death while an Ante was laid low in Carthage for real. The way I see it both [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] should be, and are, dead and gone regardless of what conspiracy and paranoid beliefs about them is propagated. It turned out that neither of them really was the kind of natural force they imagine themselves to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Brujah may very well not be dead either. Gehenna had him survive using Temporis and then hating all his childer (and the True Brujah even more than the main line). In general, most of the supposedly slain Antes turn out to be alive or not-quite-dead, depending on the source.<br /> <br /> And that's how it should be. We should never know exactly which Antes are still alive and which ones are gone for good. The only problem is that some stories of X or Y surviving were repeated more clearly and consistently than others, which gives the impression that those events might be more canon than the alternative legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:22:56-07:00","id":1480782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480723#post1480723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(although, to be fair, the fear of the &quot;Antes&quot; come much more from their sheer power and their will to destroy/subjugate the world than from their looks, as in some cases nobody would even know who or where the Ante is and that is fearsome as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, my point is more on being able to picture anything related to their activities than picturing their images themselves.<br /> <br /> Set is a good example in this because, while we half-expect him to look like your stereotypical Setite, just a bald Egyptian with maybe some snake features, we're not actually ever given much description, and what we have is just Setite-looking. But we have a better grasp of what his dominion can look like (or what we can fear from it) from his many recorded actions and sorcery.<br /> <br /> Giving great but specific goals beyond Gehenna/Jyhad, even if uncertain and self-contradicting, to the Antes is a great way to mix what we're able to imagine from their Disciplines and clans and make a mental image of a more palpable threat. I agree that [Lasombra] is a very good example, too, although I still think it needs a bit more, and I purposefully left out Giovanny and Tremere since they're not Antes even if 3rd Generation, otherwise they would have the advantage of far more complex and immediate plots to help imagine what they could do.<br /> <br /> Take [Ventrue] as an example. It's implied that if they survived, they can be a collective consciousness surreptitiously taking over everyone and guiding us to their goal of... what? I mean, the idea of a being so powerful it literally made the entire world into a hive mind without we even noticing that our wills are constantly reshaped is terrifying. But without a goal to this will except somehow the world as is is already their goal is kinda bland, makes it lose the punch quickly if you pay attention to the idea for more than some seconds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480728#post1480728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] I personally dislike that they, unlike [Brujah], [Ventrue] and some more, could totally cheat death while an Ante was laid low in Carthage for real. The way I see it both [Tzimisce] and [Lasombra] should be, and are, dead and gone regardless of what conspiracy and paranoid beliefs about them is propagated. It turned out that neither of them really was the kind of natural force they imagine themselves to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree, though for [Tzimisce] specifically I find their story of cheating death a good one. [Lasombra], not so much.<br /> <br /> But my point is less the reality of the Antes and more their legends. The reality can be quite different, and to me it actually works better with a lot more of mundanity to it. [Lasombra] died of starvation from exploring the Abyss, leaving a desperate but powerful Ghoul, and Gratiano don't want to reveal that the clan feared the Wizard of Oz for centuries. [Tzimisce] is stuck with a mediocre Path rating because he's too egotistical to Transcend. Arikel/Ishtar dropped the Jyhad completely and helps artists unionize through the internet, a real challenge and better use for her skills. Absimilliard lives in a cave near to a port and drinks on drug users exclusively and frequently, for no sustenance, just the kicks.<br /> <br /> For whatever the truth about them is worth, these are Antes you can put in front of your PCs with their full power and knowledge without fear of the chronicle getting out of hand. They can provide help or antagonize, can't be even approached in sheer power, even by Methuselahs, yet they won't just &quot;win&quot; by showing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T22:57:47-07:00","id":1480803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480782#post1480782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, my point is more on being able to picture anything related to their activities than picturing their images themselves.<br /> <br /> Set is a good example in this because, while we half-expect him to look like your stereotypical Setite, just a bald Egyptian with maybe some snake features, we're not actually ever given much description, and what we have is just Setite-looking. But we have a better grasp of what his dominion can look like (or what we can fear from it) from his many recorded actions and sorcery.<br /> <br /> Giving great but specific goals beyond Gehenna/Jyhad, even if uncertain and self-contradicting, to the Antes is a great way to mix what we're able to imagine from their Disciplines and clans and make a mental image of a more palpable threat. I agree that [Lasombra] is a very good example, too, although I still think it needs a bit more, and I purposefully left out Giovanny and Tremere since they're not Antes even if 3rd Generation, otherwise they would have the advantage of far more complex and immediate plots to help imagine what they could do.<br /> <br /> Take [Ventrue] as an example. It's implied that if they survived, they can be a collective consciousness surreptitiously taking over everyone and guiding us to their goal of... what? I mean, the idea of a being so powerful it literally made the entire world into a hive mind without we even noticing that our wills are constantly reshaped is terrifying. But without a goal to this will except somehow the world as is is already their goal is kinda bland, makes it lose the punch quickly if you pay attention to the idea for more than some seconds.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mostly agree, though for [Tzimisce] specifically I find their story of cheating death a good one. [Lasombra], not so much.<br /> <br /> But my point is less the reality of the Antes and more their legends. The reality can be quite different, and to me it actually works better with a lot more of mundanity to it. [Lasombra] died of starvation from exploring the Abyss, leaving a desperate but powerful Ghoul, and Gratiano don't want to reveal that the clan feared the Wizard of Oz for centuries. [Tzimisce] is stuck with a mediocre Path rating because he's too egotistical to Transcend. Arikel/Ishtar dropped the Jyhad completely and helps artists unionize through the internet, a real challenge and better use for her skills. Absimilliard lives in a cave near to a port and drinks on drug users exclusively and frequently, for no sustenance, just the kicks.<br /> <br /> For whatever the truth about them is worth, these are Antes you can put in front of your PCs with their full power and knowledge without fear of the chronicle getting out of hand. They can provide help or antagonize, can't be even approached in sheer power, even by Methuselahs, yet they won't just &quot;win&quot; by showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I see, now I understand better what you meant. On a side note, Set would likely be a blue-eyed redhead lol. But then again, when I talked about &quot;imagery&quot; I also meant what we can expect from their dominion, but also what they look like, as it's part of the concept. I couldn't agree more with what you said regarding that it would be great to give them more palpable goals and actions in the past, so we can know what to expect from them. I made a joke about Lestat, but I think we're basically talking about the same concept. The legends associated with them and that helps us buld the &quot;imagery&quot; associated with them and their dominion/goals could be more developped, as sometimes I'd say I could fear more Augustus or Tremere, than the old antes, especifically because these have more palpable goals and represent a more &quot;present&quot; threat as they are far more active and have more of their activities &quot;documented&quot;, so that they feel more &quot;real&quot;. I see your point and I agree, I just sometimes think Tziisce went over the top with its representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T03:53:44-07:00","id":1480822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480782#post1480782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my point is less the reality of the Antes and more their legends. The reality can be quite different, and to me it actually works better with a lot more of mundanity to it. [Lasombra] died of starvation from exploring the Abyss, leaving a desperate but powerful Ghoul, and Gratiano don't want to reveal that the clan feared the Wizard of Oz for centuries. [Tzimisce] is stuck with a mediocre Path rating because he's too egotistical to Transcend. Arikel/Ishtar dropped the Jyhad completely and helps artists unionize through the internet, a real challenge and better use for her skills. Absimilliard lives in a cave near to a port and drinks on drug users exclusively and frequently, for no sustenance, just the kicks.<br /> <br /> For whatever the truth about them is worth, these are Antes you can put in front of your PCs with their full power and knowledge without fear of the chronicle getting out of hand. They can provide help or antagonize, can't be even approached in sheer power, even by Methuselahs, yet they won't just &quot;win&quot; by showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's how I attend approach the 3rd, I also tend to confirm some of them as dead. Lasombaras survival isn't very interesting as the slightly amusing morality play of his entire outlook being a mistake because he's ultimatly a selfish asshole In a surprisingly mundane context.<br /> I actually personal canon that Ishtar committed suicide pretty early on. Largely out of fear of what she was becoming.<br /> <br /> But I do very much tend to have them persuing their own aghendas and interests rather than being some abstract force of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-12-2022, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T15:29:19-07:00","id":1480870,"title":"","content":"Like I said before I'm a fan of the Old Clan Tzismce and saw something that clicked with me and like the notion of them being seekers of estoric knowledge, impeccable manners and making no bones about what they are. The later modern branch left me cold and not worth the effort to use as npc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Made a careless mistake. 05-12-2022, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T16:16:02-07:00","id":1480880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480870#post1480870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said before I'm a fan of the Old Clan Tzismce and saw something that clicked with me and like the notion of them being seekers of estoric knowledge, impeccable manners and making no bones about what they are. The later modern branch left me cold and not worth the effort to use as npc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also like the old clan better, in general. Though I think it would have been perhaps a good idea to make Koldunism their clan discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T13:38:49-07:00","id":1480999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480880#post1480880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I also like the old clan better, in general. Though I think it would have been perhaps a good idea to make Koldunism their clan discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div> What discipline would Koldunism replace if you had your way? I like the clan spread of Animalism, Auspex and Dominate for the group myself and only a few would try to learn to basics of this type of blood magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T14:06:50-07:00","id":1481007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480999#post1480999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What discipline would Koldunism replace if you had your way? I like the clan spread of Animalism, Auspex and Dominate for the group myself and only a few would try to learn to basics of this type of blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say it would be better to replace dominate with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T19:58:43-07:00","id":1481037,"title":"","content":"I don't think Dominate is a good fit for the clan (it may be for some of them, but they can buy as Out-of-Clan), but I wouldn't make any sorcery In-Clan for anyone, specially in V20, but even in V5. I think that being given explicit access to it if they want to learn is perfect already for all the &quot;sorcerous&quot; clans and bloodlines;<br /> <br /> Personally I have nothing against Vicissitude, but taken out of the picture the best replacement is certainly Protean, not Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:19:24-07:00","id":1481076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481037#post1481037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Dominate is a good fit for the clan (it may be for some of them, but they can buy as Out-of-Clan), but I wouldn't make any sorcery In-Clan for anyone, specially in V20, but even in V5. I think that being given explicit access to it if they want to learn is perfect already for all the &quot;sorcerous&quot; clans and bloodlines;<br /> <br /> Personally I have nothing against Vicissitude, but taken out of the picture the best replacement is certainly Protean, not Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember the Old Clan is pretty much a small potent bloodline that hates Vicissitude with a passion and I don't see a problem of them having Dominate in place of it. What is your reasons for seeing it as a poor fit; if you don't mind me asking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T11:07:30-07:00","id":1481096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481076#post1481076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the Old Clan is pretty much a small potent bloodline that hates Vicissitude with a passion and I don't see a problem of them having Dominate in place of it. What is your reasons for seeing it as a poor fit; if you don't mind me asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never been a fan of the Old Clan's spread, or even of them as a separate bloodline for that matter.<br /> <br /> And I don't think Dominate a good fit for isolated lords that work more through the notion of ownership and/or tradition than by virtue of their social skills, and frequently don't even command personally. While not a social skill itself, Dominate is about personal presence and imposing will, and about giving orders directly.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are distant, isolated lords focused on personal development, and their relationship with their servants is more like an extension of their relationship to the land itself, from all perspectives. They rule because they rule the land, because that's their place and identity, you obey because you belong to that land, that's <b>your</b> place and identity, intertwined in many ways with one another, and you never need to meet or like each other to know and follow your roles, and breaking this ancient pact isn't so much impossible, but just fraught with danger.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of them <b>are</b> more direct in their lordship and do benefit of Dominate both personally and thematically. But then OoC is good enough an option, Dominate isn't a particularly hard Discipline to learn and may even be specially easy among them, but still OoC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T18:20:00-07:00","id":1481154,"title":"","content":"I wonder if how applying the concept of Charm Modes from <b>Exalted: Essence</b> could work here. The idea there is that certain (all?) Universal Charms, which all Exalt types have access too, have alternate and/or augmenting effects depending on the user\u2019s Exalt type.<br /> <br /> So where base Animalism only affects mundane animals one at a time in an immediate and physical way, Tzimisce Animalism can target humans (making it pseudo-Dominate), Gangrel Animalism gets the \u2018inner Beast\u2019 and frenzy manipulating powers (invoking the Berserker legends, tying them back to Odin and co.), Nosferatu Animalism targets entire swarms at once (imagine hordes of rats, cats, roaches etc.),<br /> Ravnos Animalism conjures animate illusions of animals and humans, and so on.<br /> <br /> Diablerie could grant access to these \u2018Clan Modes\u2019, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T20:16:56-07:00","id":1481159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481037#post1481037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Dominate is a good fit for the clan (it may be for some of them, but they can buy as Out-of-Clan), but I wouldn't make any sorcery In-Clan for anyone, specially in V20, but even in V5. I think that being given explicit access to it if they want to learn is perfect already for all the &quot;sorcerous&quot; clans and bloodlines;<br /> <br /> Personally I have nothing against Vicissitude, but taken out of the picture the best replacement is certainly Protean, not Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while I on one side, certainly don't have a problem with the Old Clan Tzimisce having Koldunism as a clan discipline, specially since both the Assamite and the Tremere have it as clan discipline and not giving it to the Old Clan would only mean it costs more xp, what is in turn almost completely irrelevant to the setting and only relevant to a PC wanting to learn it. On the other side, I think Protean is one of the best disciplines in the game and certainly a very interesting and fitting one to give to the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T11:57:10-07:00","id":1481386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481096#post1481096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the Old Clan's spread, or even of them as a separate bloodline for that matter.<br /> <br /> And I don't think Dominate a good fit for isolated lords that work more through the notion of ownership and/or tradition than by virtue of their social skills, and frequently don't even command personally. While not a social skill itself, Dominate is about personal presence and imposing will, and about giving orders directly.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are distant, isolated lords focused on personal development, and their relationship with their servants is more like an extension of their relationship to the land itself, from all perspectives. They rule because they rule the land, because that's their place and identity, you obey because you belong to that land, that's <b>your</b> place and identity, intertwined in many ways with one another, and you never need to meet or like each other to know and follow your roles, and breaking this ancient pact isn't so much impossible, but just fraught with danger.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of them <b>are</b> more direct in their lordship and do benefit of Dominate both personally and thematically. But then OoC is good enough an option, Dominate isn't a particularly hard Discipline to learn and may even be specially easy among them, but still OoC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True I do have one Tzimisce npc who is going to have strong knowledge of the Presence discipline that is perculating in my mind right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T12:29:17-07:00","id":1481393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480782#post1480782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> But my point is less the reality of the Antes and more their legends. The reality can be quite different, and to me it actually works better with a lot more of mundanity to it. [Lasombra] died of starvation from exploring the Abyss, leaving a desperate but powerful Ghoul, and Gratiano don't want to reveal that the clan feared the Wizard of Oz for centuries. [Tzimisce] is stuck with a mediocre Path rating because he's too egotistical to Transcend. Arikel/Ishtar dropped the Jyhad completely and helps artists unionize through the internet, a real challenge and better use for her skills. Absimilliard lives in a cave near to a port and drinks on drug users exclusively and frequently, for no sustenance, just the kicks.<br /> <br /> For whatever the truth about them is worth, these are Antes you can put in front of your PCs with their full power and knowledge without fear of the chronicle getting out of hand. They can provide help or antagonize, can't be even approached in sheer power, even by Methuselahs, yet they won't just &quot;win&quot; by showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always head-cannoned that the ventrue antedeluvian had just abandoned the jyhad early on and wants nothing to do with their clan as a whole. Whenever I run a gehenna scenario I just have them as an easter egg at a coffee shop somewhere during the chronicle, if the PCs interact with them they get a dominate augmented middle finger and wake up from a daze 2 minutes later standing in the same spot with no onw around.<br /> <br /> This has slowly snowballed into a theory about ante's &quot;Dying&quot; essentially being code for them retiring from the Jyhad, except Cappadocius. Cappadocius just messed up Bad and is stuck somewhere between dead/undead/alive because They, their loyal childer, and the Giovanni all somehow managed to fail at their conflicting goals at the same time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T01:33:55-07:00","id":1481518,"title":"","content":"I think my issue with modern Tzimisce is not what their character concepts are. There's nothing wrong, I think, with having sadistic torturers or callous researchers or lords of fiefdoms or splatterpunk cannon fodder. That's all fine, as far as it goes.<br /> <br /> It's that there's so rarely anything outside of that. That their concepts are very narrow.<br /> <br /> The problem that the Souleaters presented wasn't really the Souleaters themselves. It was that it established the Tzimisce as being subtly &quot;wrong&quot;. In a way that the Clan didn't shake even when Souleaters as a concept were quietly dropped. Whether it's spiritual parasites, the malign influence of Kupala, or the machinations of [Tzimisce], the whole Clan is pigeon-holed into being monstrous. That they can never have defensible motivations. That even if they try to be positive, it must be twisted somehow. You can't have the horror just from the fact they're a blood-drinking necro-parasite, they also need to be maladjusted or taking their actions to unhealthy places.<br /> <br /> This is largely a problem with all Vampires, of course, but it's especially apparent with Tzimisce. And <i>especially</i> especially when Vicissitude is involved.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce using their flesh-shaping powers to turn themselves or others into freaks, or to use their powers to hurt people, is not, as stated previously, the problem. The problem is that's all Tzimisce are allowed to be. And if they're not that, they're in thrall to the &quot;Noble Monster&quot; archetype. Which, again, not a bad idea, but limiting if that's ALL they can be.<br /> <br /> The fact that Vicissitude is only used for horror is kind of problematic. The ability to change yourself can only be used for evil or, begrudgingly, for base utility? Seems like the game and our fandom have missed a trick here.<br /> <br /> Ideas off the top of my head for using Vicissitude:<br /> <br /> 1) The Tzimisce is trans or genderfluid. Their ability to change themselves is a liberating power, allowing them to be whatever they want to be. It's about self-actualization, in a manner that is very rooted in the human experience. And they can further grant this gift for others, whether living or undead. Imagine a Tzimisce whose ghouls or Herd are trans people, marginalized or living on the street, that they grant miraculous transformations to when their own home situation would never allow them to transition. Is this a good idea? Probably not. But it's something a Tzimisce could do, if they were looking to humanity (and Humanity) rather than cutting themselves off from it.<br /> <br /> 2) A Tzimisce who, every time they accidentally kill someone from overfeeding, feels compelled to take on that person's identity for a time. They believe or even just feel like they're obligated to put their victim to rest, to exorcise their possessing spirit through emulating their life. Sleeping in their bed. Eating their favorite foods (assume the Tzimisce has the Eat Food merit). Watching their favorite movies, and reading their favorite books. Publishing their unfinished manuscript. Making peace with their loved ones. Making sure their pets have a home. <i>Getting revenge on their enemies</i>. And when the Tzimisce believes they've sufficiently placated the memory of this person whose life they stole, they give them a funeral and discard their face.<br /> <br /> 3) A penitent Tzimisce who marks their body with a physical symbol of their transgressions. They craft them on when they commit the sin, and only remove it when they've properly atoned. Their body is often a quilt of scars, knotwork, and the faces of anguished victims. They're on a personal crusade, trying to do enough good to level out the harm they've done.<br /> <br /> 4) They commit daring crimes or scandalous acts, while wearing the faces of corrupt businessmen or politicians. Just in the hopes of causing problems for them. It doesn't matter if nothing comes of it. Even legitimate crimes go unpunished. It's that their names have been dragged through the mud, as they ought to be. Keeping the spotlight on folks who would rather be forgotten by the public. (This is also not limited to mortals, either. They could attract all kinds of negative attention to powerful Kindred, whether via the public or for vampire hunters.)<br /> <br /> 5) A Tzimisce that scares people away from places haunted or stalked by monsters far worse than them. Assumes the appearance of the most disturbing horror movie monsters, and finds people sneaking around where they're not supposed to go. Giving them a good scare, so they avoid the place like the plague. OR you have a Tzimisce that tries to revitalize the local economy by taking the form of a cryptid, and make scattered appearances (never close enough to really be seen). Animals can be controlled for this purpose as well, since people will readily mistake a barn owl for a Moth Man all on their own. If the Tzimisce can get TV programs devoted to gormless TV crews looking for monsters that (mostly) don't exist, that puts the city back on the map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T11:54:25-07:00","id":1481546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) A Tzimisce who, every time they accidentally kill someone from overfeeding, feels compelled to take on that person's identity for a time. They believe or even just feel like they're obligated to put their victim to rest, to exorcise their possessing spirit through emulating their life. Sleeping in their bed. Eating their favorite foods (assume the Tzimisce has the Eat Food merit). Watching their favorite movies, and reading their favorite books. Publishing their unfinished manuscript. Making peace with their loved ones. Making sure their pets have a home. <i>Getting revenge on their enemies</i>. And when the Tzimisce believes they've sufficiently placated the memory of this person whose life they stole, they give them a funeral and discard their face. </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting take on the Tzimisce. I agree that, even more than the other cainites, the Tzimisce are viewed as irredeemable monsters and it kind of limit their options as characters, even more so when we're talking about PC characters, although it can be argued that the same often apply to many clans. One thing I might add is that there are many Tzimisce PCs who like to have a&quot; perfect form&quot; (i.e. have max appearance), instead of looking monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-20-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T12:17:29-07:00","id":1481547,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m tinkering with Late Antiquity VtM at the moment, and based on the Dark Ages Dracul confirming some of the Old Clan narrative that Vicissistude hasn\u2019t always been so proliferate through the Clan (but still wanting it around if only for some Dracones to make monsters out of mythology), what I\u2019m thinking is giving them the Old Clan Discipline spred with both Vicissitude and a form of broader animistic blood sorcery that incorporates Koldunic sorcery being available to purchase at out of Clan cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T13:28:54-07:00","id":1481555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481546#post1481546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a very interesting take on the Tzimisce. I agree that, even more than the other cainites, the Tzimisce are viewed as irredeemable monsters and it kind of limit their options as characters, even more so when we're talking about PC characters, although it can be argued that the same often apply to many clans. One thing I might add is that there are many Tzimisce PCs who like to have a&amp;quot; perfect form&amp;quot; (i.e. have max appearance), instead of looking monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that &quot;monstrous/inhuman&quot; and &quot;beautiful&quot; are not necessarily mutually exclusive. Sascha Vykos is statted with more than 5 dots in Appearance but has generally been depicted as quite inhuman looking. My understanding is that plenty of Tzimisce try and appear both monstrous and beautiful, more beautiful than is humanly possible even, through Vicissitude. <br /> <br /> All of them are trying to find a &quot;perfect form,&quot; but they have different criteria for what that means. There are as many trying for angelic beauty as hideous monstrosity; what tends to be consistent is the inhumanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:34:01-07:00","id":1481564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481555#post1481555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth noting that &quot;monstrous/inhuman&quot; and &quot;beautiful&quot; are not necessarily mutually exclusive. Sascha Vykos is statted with more than 5 dots in Appearance but has generally been depicted as quite inhuman looking. My understanding is that plenty of Tzimisce try and appear both monstrous and beautiful, more beautiful than is humanly possible even, through Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> All of them are trying to find a &quot;perfect form,&quot; but they have different criteria for what that means. There are as many trying for angelic beauty as hideous monstrosity; what tends to be consistent is the inhumanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are certainly not &quot;mutually exclusive&quot;, I just meant that there are many Tzimisce who look very beautiful and not monstrous. Gesu , from Constantinople is a good example that comes to mind. Also, I talk mostly about my personal experience, many players use Vicissitude as &quot;plastic surgery&quot; to make their characters aesthetically perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:42:28-07:00","id":1481565,"title":"","content":"There's always been a tendency to code certain disciplines as evil, and it's always been strange. Necromancy, Quietus, and Viccissitude top the list. Necromancy has always been coded as evil, and this tendency has gotten worse this edition with the mere use of Oblivion creating a significant risk of stains even if it is used to save puppies and orphans.<br /> <br /> I've always found it strange, since all vampiric powers are used to aid in the hunting and eating of humans. Auspex tracks humans, checks if there are witnesses nearby, and discovers any weaknesses that might be used to manipulate the prey. Fortitude shrugs off the counter-attacks of the prey as you try to eat them. Potence lets you overpower the prey and beat them into submission so you can eat them. Celerity allows you pounce on the prey before they can escape. Dominate and Presence are both mind-rape performed to control the prey so you can eat them. There are no nice disciplines. They are, every last one of them, weapons to eat people with.<br /> <br /> Yet Necromancy/Oblivion, Quietus, and Viccissitude are the officially evil disciplines. These are the disciplines that get coded as something inherently worse than what normal vampires use. They seem to represent Death, Poison, and Corruption in the minds of the writers, and this is somehow worse than violating someone's mind with Dominate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T16:35:16-07:00","id":1481567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481564#post1481564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are certainly not &amp;quot;mutually exclusive&amp;quot;, I just meant that there are many Tzimisce who look very beautiful and not monstrous. Gesu , from Constantinople is a good example that comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, he doesn't look monstrous until you see Lillian's face embedded in his chest, that's pretty monstrous to me even if he still looks beautiful and human otherwise.<br /> <br /> But I get what you mean. IIRC Damek Ruthven only used his Vicissitude to increase his size, but otherwise looked as human as any other vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T17:56:13-07:00","id":1481571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481565#post1481565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always been a tendency to code certain disciplines as evil, and it's always been strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not forget Obtenebration, and sometimes even Serpentis, because Snake Protean is EVIL.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the authors sometimes lost track that the game was already about monsters and tried to outdo themselves, and the Tzimisce are among the most frequent to be singled out for the job, with Vicissitude being somehow more horrific than other Disciplines because... reasons.<br /> <br /> A lot of this also have to do with traditions from American/British literature and fiction the authors frequently followed by heart, even if not always it made sense for, again, a game of monsters, much less when other cultural influences started to come in (or at least their aesthetics).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481567#post1481567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Damek Ruthven only used his Vicissitude to increase his size, but otherwise looked as human as any other vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>His childer Danika doesn't seems to have used it at all on her own appearance, although she may have reverted it after becoming Inconnu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T18:06:15-07:00","id":1481573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he doesn't look monstrous until you see Lillian's face embedded in his chest </div> </div> </div>Many Tzimisce are romantic (Velya is another one that comes to mind hahaha), it's understandable, I don't think it's monstrous at all lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His childer Danika doesn't seems to have used it at all on her own appearance, although she may have reverted it after becoming Inconnu. </div> </div> </div>Also, her child Anastazi used his Vicissitude to look like a paragon of male beauty, not monstrous at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T03:15:02-07:00","id":1481587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481565#post1481565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always been a tendency to code certain disciplines as evil, and it's always been strange. Necromancy, Quietus, and Viccissitude top the list. Necromancy has always been coded as evil, and this tendency has gotten worse this edition with the mere use of Oblivion creating a significant risk of stains even if it is used to save puppies and orphans.<br /> <br /> I've always found it strange, since all vampiric powers are used to aid in the hunting and eating of humans. Auspex tracks humans, checks if there are witnesses nearby, and discovers any weaknesses that might be used to manipulate the prey. Fortitude shrugs off the counter-attacks of the prey as you try to eat them. Potence lets you overpower the prey and beat them into submission so you can eat them. Celerity allows you pounce on the prey before they can escape. Dominate and Presence are both mind-rape performed to control the prey so you can eat them. There are no nice disciplines. They are, every last one of them, weapons to eat people with.<br /> <br /> Yet Necromancy/Oblivion, Quietus, and Viccissitude are the officially evil disciplines. These are the disciplines that get coded as something inherently worse than what normal vampires use. They seem to represent Death, Poison, and Corruption in the minds of the writers, and this is somehow worse than violating someone's mind with Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I always thought this was weak writting, not so much for the assumption certain disciplines are 'bad' but because of the fallacy some arnt. I tend to hint that all the disciplines are metaphysical traps it's just some are more overt than others or not at all depending on who you ask.<br /> <br /> Oblivion following of this mindset in v5 is probably one of the editions biggest gaffes. For both mechanical and thematic reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T07:36:30-07:00","id":1481597,"title":"","content":"The idea that if you code some vampiric powers as extra heinous it somehow exonerates other vampiric powers seems like a fallacy to me. That's like saying that you cannot highlight chlorofluorocarbons as extra damaging to the ozone layer without also talking about all other ozone-depleting substances. If something is called out as particularly destructive, that does not make less destructive but still harmful things okay.<br /> <br /> I can't think of examples from the books that treat Quietus as an especially wicked set of powers, but I have no problem with Vicissitude and Necromancy as 'extra evil' disciplines. Like I've argued in this thread and elsewhere in the past, original flavor Vicissitude is pretty much just straight up Wyrm/Bane/fomor influence, so the idea that employing it would take a toll on the user physically, mentally, and spiritually is a no-brainer to me. Likewise, the World of Darkness has traditionally treated Necromancy as the power of commanding, binding, and torturing immortal souls. Even the mummy variety of Necromancy in the original supplement put the user at risk of Derangement rolls -- and mummies were far less bad guys than vampires, as a general thing.<br /> <br /> If the writers want to highlight powers such as these as particularly damaging to one's sanity or morality, that seems to me like a perfectly justifiable rather than a strange choice. I certainly can't agree that it's a sign of &quot;weak&quot; writing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 05-21-2022, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T09:13:33-07:00","id":1481604,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Herr Meister;n1481573]<br /> <br /> Many Tzimisce are romantic (Velya is another one that comes to mind hahaha), it's understandable, I don't think it's monstrous at all lol<br /> <br /> Velya was a demented character for sure with his write up and I couldn;t get the image of his bride attached to him out of my head and the same with Gesu having the face of Lillian on his chest and driving a further wedge between him and his brother.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T02:53:33-07:00","id":1481650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481597#post1481597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the writers want to highlight powers such as these as particularly damaging to one's sanity or morality, that seems to me like a perfectly justifiable rather than a strange choice. I certainly can't agree that it's a sign of &quot;weak&quot; writing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to disagree with you on this, that certain powers are innately evil and that using them makes you evil. It's an overly simplistic approach to morality (see examples here: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BadPowersBadPeople\" target=\"_blank\">Bad Powers, Bad People - TV Tropes</a>), and prevents any interesting nuance from becoming a story.<br /> <br /> As an example compare the one ring in Lord of the Rings with the Dresden files cursed coins. Everyone in LotR treats the one ring like toxic waste and anyone who uses it <i>inevitably </i>pays for it. Whereas in the Dresden files the cursed coins are treated by everyone as toxic waste, but when Harry picks one up we have a several book 'struggle against temptation' story that ends really well.<br /> <br /> Enforcing that certain powers <b>inevitably </b>corrupt their user takes away player agency, and to me, a good story comes from giving players the agency to struggle with the moral nuances of powers that could corrupt them.<br /> <br /> See alos: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilMakesYouUgly\" target=\"_blank\">Evil Makes You Ugly - TV Tropes</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 05-22-2022, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T04:23:21-07:00","id":1481651,"title":"","content":"The idea that WoD has always depicted Necromancy as evil is false. Mage: The Ascension has a whole Tradition - the Euthanatos (Chakravanti) - that are all about death magic. Yet they, among other Mage groups, show the complicated facets of death arts, and how Necromancy doesn't need to be adversarial or malicious. It's only bad if the Necromancer chooses to use their powers in a way that causes harm or forces ghosts to do their bidding.<br /> <br /> (Yes, this is the same Tradition that has ritualized murder as one of their cornerstones. But even then, their killings are done with noble intent. Showing a nuanced approach to ethics that the World of Darkness is interested in exploring.)<br /> <br /> Bringing us back around to Vicissitude, I think while flesh-crafting is uniquely squicky and open to abuse, this does not require that it must be an evil Discipline. It's only our preconceptions that designate it so. It's to presuppose they are uniquely transgressive, and then work backwards from that conclusion. It's the WoD equivalent of early D&amp;D designating the use of Poison as a categorically Evil aligned act. It's all arbitrary, and frankly limits what we can do with characters.<br /> <br /> Once again, the existence of Tzimisce that use flesh-crafting exclusively for evil, or obeying deeply anti-social ethical codes, is not a bad thing. That's fine. I take issue with this being the only mode one can take with Vicissitude, or any other Discipline for that matter. Baking a moral judgement about the Disciplines into their supernatural make-up, in-universe, doesn't meaningfully add story possibilities. The fucked-up applications of Vicissitude can stand perfectly well on their own, without adding to it a spiritual corruption inherent to its very use. The latter only subtracts the number of stories that can be told about Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> And, as I've said many times over the years, my contention is that, all else being equal, more potential stories is better than fewer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T05:09:56-07:00","id":1481653,"title":"","content":"In the earlier editions of VtM at least, Necromancy was always given a fairly negative light. Though to be fair vampires are more monstrous than Mages, so most vampiric powers tend to be presented as more monstrous or spooky or evil than Mage powers. And on top of that, by far and away the most common practitioners of Necromancy are the Giovanni, who are especially messed up, even by Vampire standards. Their Necromancy tends to focus more on the enslavement of ghosts and this tended to color the presentation of Necromancy (which, by default, was coming out of the D&amp;D tradition where Necromancy already had a pretty negative coloring).<br /> <br /> Beyond the Giovanni we got a few bits and pieces about Setite Necromancy, but it's generally not much better. And Nagaraja were maybe worse than the Giovanni in some respects. And then the Cappadocians weren't horrible, but they practiced Mortis which was kind of puesdo-Necromancy and they were extinct by the modern nights. Really the &quot;nicest&quot; Necromancers in the modern VtM setting were the Samedi, as the books went out of the way to note that they tended to view their ghosts as valuable partners rather than slaves like the Giovanni. But Samedi were pretty darn rare and definitely not the typical users of Necromancy.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until Dark Ages Revised, where we got an expansion on Necromancy to make it comparable to Thaumaturgy and Mortis/Thanatosis got rolled into Necromancy, that Necromancy finally got a wide enough net to have expanded past the Giovanni and it stopped being a mostly creepy/evil Discipline. And then V20 started to expand on that, giving Necromancy to the Kiasyd and others.<br /> <br /> These days I feel that Necromancy isn't much worse than Dominate or Presence or other Disciplines but I believe it's also the Discipline that has evolved and changed the most since its' original introduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T06:22:32-07:00","id":1481655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481650#post1481650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got to disagree with you on this, that certain powers are innately evil and that using them makes you evil. It's an overly simplistic approach to morality (see examples here: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BadPowersBadPeople\" target=\"_blank\">Bad Powers, Bad People - TV Tropes</a>), and prevents any interesting nuance from becoming a story.<br /> <br /> As an example compare the one ring in Lord of the Rings with the Dresden files cursed coins. Everyone in LotR treats the one ring like toxic waste and anyone who uses it <i>inevitably </i>pays for it. Whereas in the Dresden files the cursed coins are treated by everyone as toxic waste, but when Harry picks one up we have a several book 'struggle against temptation' story that ends really well.<br /> <br /> Enforcing that certain powers <b>inevitably </b>corrupt their user takes away player agency, and to me, a good story comes from giving players the agency to struggle with the moral nuances of powers that could corrupt them.<br /> <br /> See alos: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilMakesYouUgly\" target=\"_blank\">Evil Makes You Ugly - TV Tropes</a></div> </div> </div> </div>...Are you holding up <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> as an example of weak writing without any interesting nuance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The entire point of the One Ring is that it can only work on what is already there within each person. Every character, from the greatness of Galadriel to the humility of Samwise Gamgee, has a wish list of the changes they would like to see in the world. If the Wise treat the Ring like 'toxic waste', it's only because they understand most deeply -- through millennia of bitter experience in the case of the Elves -- that the act of imposing your individual will upon the world is almost indistinguishable from the act of imposing your will upon other creatures. Sauron is simply the end point of that path, but even he was not created evil. He is the natural desire to organize the world according to one's personal preferences, given mythic proportions. Tolkien himself was an anarchist, and was of the opinion that more or less anyone who <i>wants</i> a position of authority is unfit to hold a position of authority. Although JRRT was not the kind of writer to put his political views front and center in his works, and 'cordially disliked' allegory, his legendarium is nevertheless deeply concerned with questions of morality and moral agency.<br /> <br /> In addition to its linguistic complexity and mythological depth, <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> is a mature work about power and the desire to wield it. The popular conception that the book is nothing more than a simplistic black-and-white morality play says more about the attentiveness of most readers than it does about the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T12:26:29-07:00","id":1481680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481650#post1481650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got to disagree with you on this, that certain powers are innately evil and that using them makes you evil. It's an overly simplistic approach to morality (see examples here: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BadPowersBadPeople&amp;quot;]Bad</a> Powers, Bad People - TV Tropes[/URL]), and prevents any interesting nuance from becoming a story.<br /> <br /> As an example compare the one ring in Lord of the Rings with the Dresden files cursed coins. Everyone in LotR treats the one ring like toxic waste and anyone who uses it <i>inevitably </i>pays for it. Whereas in the Dresden files the cursed coins are treated by everyone as toxic waste, but when Harry picks one up we have a several book 'struggle against temptation' story that ends really well.<br /> <br /> Enforcing that certain powers <b>inevitably </b>corrupt their user takes away player agency, and to me, a good story comes from giving players the agency to struggle with the moral nuances of powers that could corrupt them.<br /> <br /> See alos: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilMakesYouUgly&amp;quot;]Evil</a> Makes You Ugly - TV Tropes[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Sam gandhi use it and didnt paid anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T13:39:23-07:00","id":1481684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481655#post1481655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Are you holding up <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> as an example of weak writing without any interesting nuance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That may have been a bad example and I agree, yet you're just avoiding the criticism.<br /> <br /> Setting aside that the One Ring has a completely different story function from VtM's Disciplines, we must evaluate such properties within the context of the game, an RPG about &quot;damned&quot; monsters with themes of the relativity of morality and the error of believing in absolutes.<br /> <br /> As an RPG it must be open to many stories, by many people. Stating some powers as intrinsically malignant instead of just leaning to corruption greatly limits how many stories you can tell with them and how many distinct characters you can build with them. More than that, it eliminates the morality dubiousness, making for a situation where right and wrong become evident because they're power-coded.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how much this kind of coding works in Tolkien (and I'm a <b>HUGE</b> fan of his work) or in Necroscope, it isn't even necessarily a bad thing for a given VtM chronicle, you sure can have an awesome game built over the premise that some powers are inherently damning, beyond and above being a vampire. What's a problem is building it in the setting as an unavoidable truth. <b>That</b> limits game in ways you're only ok with because <b>you</b> are not interested in <i>not</i> referencing Necroscope when the Tzimisce appears, but sucks for everyone that grew tired of this trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T14:05:41-07:00","id":1481685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481680#post1481680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sam gandhi use it and didnt paid anything</div> </div> </div> </div>Samwise Gamgee used it for an extremely brief time and his greater character quality was that he had few to no strong personal desire, much less at that moment. For the entire time Sam held the Ring, his thoughts are about others and his anguish is that he's sure he'll fail. He isn't sorry for himself, he doesn't wish praise or comfort, he only misses not knowing what's the right decision for him to make, to continue or to stay with Frodo's corpse. He's the most sincere and pure member of the Fellowship (if not without his flaws, flaws that arguably damned Gollum), also the most humble, so the only one to truly have no desire for the Ring.<br /> <br /> Even then it must be pointed that while Sam didn't resisted Frodo taking the Ring back, there was a moment that could be hesitation. And while Sam could live long years in the Middle Earth after the other Ring Bearers parted to Valinor, he too grew tired before his years (102, advanced, but not uncommon for a Hobbit to reach and still have some years to spare), something even rarer among Hobbits than humans, and as was his right went to the Undying Lands. So it can be said the price took time to show, but he paid nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T00:36:04-07:00","id":1481734,"title":"","content":"I am 100% with the OP. I my games Vicissitude has also disappeared as a Discipline and Tzimisce run with Koldunic Sorcery or Protean instead (using a caste like system). Vicissitude has remained as a Koldunic Sorcery Path, only affecting the caster's own body, removing it more grotesque uses. So now the Tzimisce is able to change their appearance, mimic some other person or even become a combat monster if they wish so, but vozdhs, human shaped screaming chairs and the like are out of the picture","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T07:40:31-07:00","id":1481752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481655#post1481655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Are you holding up <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> as an example of weak writing without any interesting nuance? <br /> <br /> says more about the attentiveness of most readers than it does about the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think I didn't notice you having a couple of digs in there...<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point wasn't at all about the <i>quality </i>of the writing but about the use of a trope on one hand and it's subversion on the other, and, as Monteparnas eloquently puts it, how that trope is possibly overused in the game system we're all involved with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T08:43:51-07:00","id":1481761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481752#post1481752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't think I didn't notice you having a couple of digs in there...<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point wasn't at all about the <i>quality </i>of the writing but about the use of a trope on one hand and it's subversion on the other, and, as Monteparnas eloquently puts it, how that trope is possibly overused in the game system we're all involved with</div> </div> </div> </div>I have had that person blocked for over half a year now, so however eloquent their arguments, I cannot see them nor comment on them.<br /> <br /> Regarding your earlier post, I simply found that contrasting an aspect of <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> with a similar plot device in <i>The Dresden Files</i> did not support your argument at all, because the One Ring does not in any way prevent &quot;any interesting nuance from becoming a story&quot;, as you put it -- far from it. If my post contained a 'dig' at someone's expense, it was directed toward the kinds of people who have only done an extremely surface level reading of <i>The Lord of the Rings</i> and are convinced that there is nothing else to the book. I did not assume that you personally fall into that category.<br /> <br /> I am not a huge fan of how roleplaying games tend to move from specific and highly flavorful ideas toward the most generic and flavorless implementations of those ideas, typically with each new edition update. Wresting Vicissitude from its original context and throwing all the lore behind it into the trash in favor of turning it into a safe and friendly 'plastic surgery power' is just one example of the phenomenon. I will grant you that the latter may be more useful for a larger number of players, but that is only a virtue if you think that <i>every</i> idea in a roleplaying game should be as open-ended and flavor-free as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T22:43:31-07:00","id":1481821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481761#post1481761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a huge fan of how roleplaying games tend to move from specific and highly flavorful ideas toward the most generic and flavorless implementations of those ideas,</div> </div> </div> </div>This<br /> Personally I loved the idea of Vicissitude was something... different<br /> Loved the Shadow Crusade idea of the Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and how a careless Deep Umbra explorer ancient. Andeleon accidently brought back something... horrible, even more terrible than the cursed monsters already tormenting Humanity. Something that was worse than <i>them</i>. Not to mention it was a nice tie-in for some crossovers, not only it was a bit similar of the Lhinanna's Ogham power-source, a fragmented nature spirit, as the Souleater was a fragment of a spiritual entity (most likely a Bane from the brood of the Eater-of-Souls), but reverse, it became stronger with every infected, it was a nice ground for mixed chorincles.<br /> Loved the idea, when they tweaked it a bittle and made Vicissitude optionally an Infection, a disease that can infect anyone that comes into contact with tainted blood. Infection is necessary for learning Vicissitude, and the degree to which one is afflicted influences the difficulty of learning levels of the Discipline. Instead of taking over a practitioner's mind, however, the disease makes it more likely those infected gain derangements.<br /> Loved the Idea, Vicissitude WAS the Tzimisce Antediluvian<br /> When The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra came and introduced the Asakku option, I was fascinated by the idea<br /> The idea, Vicissitude and Obtenebration was basically a manifestation of a Qlippothic Sphere was unique and awesome!<br /> Heck once I even made the Tzimisce Antediluvian an escaped/survived experiments/superweapon from the War of Wrath, when the Fallen line came out, making it/him the creation of the Rabisu, the Sixth House, their Lore of Flesh that bacame sentinent, Venom-like and slipped away in the final days<br /> Vicissitude had so much depth and uniquness, even if you took only the &quot;like how God shaped man from clay, the users defile this Godly act and shape the body to their own twisted immage&quot; kind of relegious explanation...<br /> Vicissitude made the Tzimisce Clan different, not just run of the mill bloodsucker (okay, vicissitude and Kuppala)<br /> It was sad to see it, like Seprentis to become lesser, and basically Protean-light","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-24-2022, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T23:26:12-07:00","id":1481826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481761#post1481761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but that is only a virtue if you think that <i>every</i> idea in a roleplaying game should be as open-ended and flavor-free as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather an overly dramatic point of view as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in the V20 rules preventing you from adding as much squick as you can tolerate to your personal flavour of campaign, it's just that many people in these times are no longer entertained by 90's style excesses, so rules systems that are agnostic about how players play a game are in many ways better than ones that proscribe forced behaviour. That's something the White Wolf crew never seem to learn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T01:01:31-07:00","id":1481832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481826#post1481826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing in the V20 rules preventing you from adding as much squick as you can tolerate to your personal flavour of campaign, it's just that many people in these times are no longer entertained by 90's style excesses, so rules systems that are agnostic about how players play a game are in many ways better than ones that proscribe forced behaviour. That's something the White Wolf crew never seem to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current topic of discussion started when it was argued that it is not only strange but also a sign of weak writing to have powers in the game that are especially perilous to use. I disagreed, and argued in favor of respecting the original intent behind such additions to the game. This is particularly relevant in the case of Vicissitude, since the only reason the discipline is even in the game today is because Steven C. Brown had a very particular idea about connecting one of his creations for <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> to the then-brand-new <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> and one of its antagonist factions.<br /> <br /> It's a bit disingenuous to suggest that if I don't care for the trend of turning specific ideas into generic ones, I can always Rule Zero away such developments. It should go without saying that each GM has the power to homebrew stuff as much as they want (and their players can stomach), but the same logic applies to each side of a discussion like this, which is why I generally prefer not to argue along those lines. To wit: if you don't like how the use of classic Vicissitude or V5 Oblivion is framed as especially damaging to the user's psyche, there's nothing preventing you from stripping away the offending flavor. Problem solved, right?<br /> <br /> I would only add that it is always easier to remove parts of a game that you don't like than it is to add specific ideas to areas of the game that the players expect to be generic. It is extremely easy to say: &quot;In this chronicle, Necromancy is <i>not</i> evil!&quot; It is quite another to pitch something like: &quot;So, in my setting, any use of Fortitude carries a heavy risk of corruption, because I have these particular ideas about the demonic influence behind Fortitude that you are just going to have to figure out ingame.&quot; The truth of the matter is that the development of ideas in roleplaying games only ever goes in one direction, away from the specific and toward the generic (or, if you prefer, agnostic). You can take that as a sign of the superiority of your preference, if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 05-24-2022, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T14:30:57-07:00","id":1481951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481821#post1481821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude made the Tzimisce Clan different, not just run of the mill bloodsucker (okay, vicissitude and Kuppala)<br /> It was sad to see it, like Seprentis to become lesser, and basically Protean-light</div> </div> </div> </div>Different and repetitive. See again all the character concepts <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> exemplified that simply can't be done with those takes on Vicissitude being canonical.<br /> <br /> You can have Vicissitude being any or all those things in your game, and you can put forward in lore as many <i>theories</i> about it being specially damning as you want, to achieve the same effect.<br /> <br /> But the problem is the proscription of behavior. To say that the games move from specific to flavorless or that you either have this power be Extra-Evil or not as a canonical truth is a fallacy. The game may present theories and options without making them a certainty. The game can present three ideas on how a given Discipline may be Horrible-Evil-Power, three on how it may be Path-To-Salvation, and then explore how those ideas affect the setting regardless of being true, because there are people that believe in then, and let the ST chose which option is the truth for their chronicle.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a>'s argument that RPGs always do this movement disregards completely the nuances of how a game evolves over time, bringing and managing ideas to help groups tell their own stories, and sometimes having to drop things because they had a bad effect on the game. Saying that is basically stating that if a big chunk of the public didn't liked an element being brought into it, they should just suck it up and go seek another game.<br /> <br /> Almost no one likes Vicissitude as a disease. Because those people had other ideas for the Discipline or the clan, and this one makes them non-viable or adds unwanted details that hurt the theme they thought of. This isn't about the idea not being good, it is about people actually liking the clan and the power and having ideas on how to use them, and this concept squashes them for very little gain.<br /> <br /> Very little gain, I repeat. The result may be a flavorful concept, but that generates a clan of repetitive character concepts that most people are uninterested in. It is the same reason they never gave a lot of space to the Salubri, my favorite clan, period: most people are uninterested in them, giving them more space would be for very little gain. I'm torn by this fact, yet I understand. Likewise they never gave space to that theory again, but news flash, it isn't an impossibility and you can still use it, it still exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T16:02:59-07:00","id":1481954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481734#post1481734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am 100% with the OP. I my games Vicissitude has also disappeared as a Discipline and Tzimisce run with Koldunic Sorcery or Protean instead (using a caste like system). Vicissitude has remained as a Koldunic Sorcery Path, only affecting the caster's own body, removing it more grotesque uses. So now the Tzimisce is able to change their appearance, mimic some other person or even become a combat monster if they wish so, but vozdhs, human shaped screaming chairs and the like are out of the picture</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, too. I ended up giving them Protean, Animalism, Presence, and Obfuscate. (All clans have 4 disciplines in my games.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T17:17:01-07:00","id":1481963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481734#post1481734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am 100% with the OP. I my games Vicissitude has also disappeared as a Discipline and Tzimisce run with Koldunic Sorcery or Protean instead (using a caste like system). Vicissitude has remained as a Koldunic Sorcery Path, only affecting the caster's own body, removing it more grotesque uses. So now the Tzimisce is able to change their appearance, mimic some other person or even become a combat monster if they wish so, but vozdhs, human shaped screaming chairs and the like are out of the picture</div> </div> </div> </div>So, at that point, why bother calling it a Tzimisce? What you have there sounds closer to a Tremere, or maybe a Setite, with some appearance altering rituals (some of which are already in game). I'm not sure I understand the appeal of choosing a clan you don't like and twisting it into something you do like by changing it's nature completely...though I appreciate the delicious allegory, considering the clan in question. Are you more interested in the soil-dependency weakness, or the in-clan cost of Protean? Or maybe just making a Tremere without the pyramid?<br /> <br /> Just seems like there are easier ways to meet that concept with the tools already presented in game rather than taking away from a clan's established lore and flavor. It's perfectly okay to not like a clan, but changing it to match more closely with another clan seems like a waste of effort when those clans already exist. Just my opinion, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T18:54:21-07:00","id":1481967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481963#post1481963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, at that point, why bother calling it a Tzimisce? What you have there sounds closer to a Tremere, or maybe a Setite, with some appearance altering rituals (some of which are already in game). I'm not sure I understand the appeal of choosing a clan you don't like and twisting it into something you do like by changing it's nature completely...though I appreciate the delicious allegory, considering the clan in question. Are you more interested in the soil-dependency weakness, or the in-clan cost of Protean? Or maybe just making a Tremere without the pyramid?<br /> <br /> Just seems like there are easier ways to meet that concept with the tools already presented in game rather than taking away from a clan's established lore and flavor. It's perfectly okay to not like a clan, but changing it to match more closely with another clan seems like a waste of effort when those clans already exist. Just my opinion, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why a Tzimisce? Because it's a Eastern European based Clan, with a feudal outlook on unlife. They are solitary territorial lords, hospitality is a sacred rule for them. They have existed for millennia and the Tremere stole their blood to become Vampires. They do not revere any Egyptian god. Their youth rebelled and went to the Sabbat at the end of the middle ages<br /> Does it just sounds as a non interesting clan because they don't have an unique discipline? Let's set rid of Toreador and Ventrue as well, them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T10:23:16-07:00","id":1482504,"title":"","content":"I did like ONE Tzimisce, Righteous Endeavor. The rest I'm mostly rather indifferent to (Andrei from Bloodlines excepted).<br /> <br /> Righteous Endeavor was this weird breath of fresh air. He didn't fling severed genitals at anyone (at least not his own), he didn't turn someone into a dress, or graft a child bride onto himself, and he didn't turn into a transexual skinhead or some mockery of a Hindu god. Righteous Endeavor was just some hypocritical, bible-thumping, asshole rapist. Aleister Crowley in puritan garb, if you will. He'd make an interesting villain, although I can't imagine how to play him as the character he's written up as without swan diving straight into wighthood.<br /> <br /> Actually, there is another exception. Lambach Ruthven is also interesting; if only because he a low-generation vampire who's both the Sire of Dracula himself, AND &quot;the Chronicler&quot; of the Eldest, and STILL manages to be quite pathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T13:14:22-07:00","id":1482646,"title":"","content":"It has occurred to me that the four original revenant families more or less embody the clan's four major archetypes.<ul><li>Brutal rural barbarians who view the world entirely in a predator vs prey dynamic with themselves at the top of the food chain and enjoy keeping/creating monstrous &quot;pets&quot;.</li> <li>Decadent hedonistic aristocrats who treat other people as their playthings and engage in bizarre fetish behavior including excessive body modification.</li> <li>Reclusive creepy mystics who keep delving into forbidden lore, ancient witchcraft and things man was not meant to know.</li> <li>Old World nobility who keep with antiquated codes of honor and behavior while caught up in a dangerous tangled web of alliances and obligations.</li> </ul><br /> (And in hindsight, I rather wish the Grimaldi had had Animalism, Auspex, and Dominate as their family discipline affinities. Not only would it have made them stand out a little less, anyone who liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand could've made the obvious parallel with the Old Clan and speculated if they were secretly their agents or something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T08:41:11-07:00","id":1487013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1480703#post1480703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think assigning Dracula's clan as Tzimisce did a disservice to Dracula, Tzimisce and the game in general. Quite a few clans embodied at least as many Dracula aspects as does Tzimisce; Gangrel, Lasombra, Nosferatu, Tremere, Ventrue...hell, even Brujah and Ravnos have distinct Dracula aspects. They should have left his clan an item of contention, with multiple clans claiming and/or blaming, as the case fit. Trying to make the Tzimisce clan fit the man or vice versa leaves something less than the sum of its parts.<br /> <br /> But it's worth noting that in the books, Dracula is not a typical Tzimisce, and is disliked/scoffed at by most of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, Dracula never should have been made a canon character. He feels far more of an amalgam of several clans, and that's what he should have been in-universe: someone's grand Masquerade breach that called out a bunch of different clans' abilities to spread knowledge far and wide.<br /> <br /> But of all the clans he could have been, Tzimisce is the weirdest, considering body horror flesh-shaping is one of the powers he very clearly does <i>not</i> have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T19:04:57-07:00","id":1487088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tiltowait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1487013#post1487013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, Dracula never should have been made a canon character. He feels far more of an amalgam of several clans, and that's what he should have been in-universe: someone's grand Masquerade breach that called out a bunch of different clans' abilities to spread knowledge far and wide.<br /> <br /> But of all the clans he could have been, Tzimisce is the weirdest, considering body horror flesh-shaping is one of the powers he very clearly does <i>not</i> have.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has the Old Tzimisce culture. That's why I say:<br /> Keep the Tzimisce, ditch Vicissitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T14:49:34-07:00","id":1487785,"title":"","content":"I have been wondering lately, how would it change the clan if the clan weakness went from two handfuls of soil to a much more inconvenient amount, like half a ton or so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:07:11-07:00","id":1487793,"title":"","content":"The Clan would be nearly unplayable in many games. If you get the amount so large, it becomes so harsh that the Clan members are easy targets for their enemies, and can't participate in many game types as PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:24:53-07:00","id":1487797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1480216-does-anyone-else-dislike-the-tzimisce?p=1481650#post1481650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got to disagree with you on this, that certain powers are innately evil and that using them makes you evil. It's an overly simplistic approach to morality (see examples here: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BadPowersBadPeople\" target=\"_blank\">Bad Powers, Bad People - TV Tropes</a>), and prevents any interesting nuance from becoming a story.<br /> <br /> As an example compare the one ring in Lord of the Rings with the Dresden files cursed coins. Everyone in LotR treats the one ring like toxic waste and anyone who uses it <i>inevitably </i>pays for it. Whereas in the Dresden files the cursed coins are treated by everyone as toxic waste, but when Harry picks one up we have a several book 'struggle against temptation' story that ends really well.<br /> <br /> Enforcing that certain powers <b>inevitably </b>corrupt their user takes away player agency, and to me, a good story comes from giving players the agency to struggle with the moral nuances of powers that could corrupt them.<br /> <br /> See alos: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilMakesYouUgly\" target=\"_blank\">Evil Makes You Ugly - TV Tropes</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with many things you said here, as I said in a post somewhere around here once, I think even vampires who got demonic investments and/or Daimoinon/Dark Thaumaturgy could &quot;redeem&quot; themselves and/or use the &quot;evil powers&quot; to fight &quot;evil&quot;, whatever it might mean. The idea of the <i>One Ring</i> though, is that, to simplify things, it kind of gives &quot;absolute power&quot; to certain powerful beings, so as Gandalf said, he would turn into a terrible tyrant if he had it even though his intentions were good. In any case, that happens because the idea of &quot;absolute power&quot; inevitably corrupts the user, but then again it becomes kind of a philosophical discussion. The thing is, in my opinion, to have certain powers should not<b> inevitably</b> corrupt the user, otherwise, as you pointed out, it would take away player AND ST agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:31:34-07:00","id":1487800,"title":"","content":"All in all, I don't like much Vicissitude (as I don't like Dementation, for instance), but not to the point of removing it from the setting, it didn't manage very well to take away the stain of being an &quot;antagonists discipline&quot;, when first published. In my opinion the worst part is the Antediluvian thing, I mean if you're going to keep the idea of Vicissitude being a disease, then I don't see why it would be better to attach it to the Antediluvian, making it an <b>\u00fcber God</b>, basically more powerful than anything else in the setting. If we're going that route, it would be simpler to keep the Black Hand's approach of it being an &quot;alien parasite&quot; lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 07-24-2022, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}